1
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:09,417
Okay, hold on,
don't shoot.

2
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:12,249
- You see where you're going?
- Mm-hmm.

3
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:13,416
Okay.

4
00:00:13,417 --> 00:00:15,333
Now, let's worry about
how you get there.

5
00:00:16,208 --> 00:00:17,417
You gotta move your foot here.

6
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:19,374
Point your toe this way.
Right here.

7
00:00:19,375 --> 00:00:21,457
Your hips here.

8
00:00:21,458 --> 00:00:22,792
Okay?

9
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:25,082
- Can you see?
- Yeah.

10
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:26,291
- Are you sure?
- Mm-hmm.

11
00:00:26,292 --> 00:00:27,707
How about now?
Can you see now?

12
00:00:27,708 --> 00:00:29,124
- No.
- How about now?

13
00:00:31,208 --> 00:00:32,292
All right.

14
00:00:32,958 --> 00:00:34,958
Ready? Three fingers.

15
00:00:35,625 --> 00:00:36,833
Nice!

16
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:40,082
Nice throw, kiddo.

17
00:00:40,083 --> 00:00:41,541
Here you go.

18
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:43,749
Hey, you guys want mayo?
Or mustard?

19
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:45,499
Or both?

20
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,624
Who puts mayo on a hot dog?

21
00:00:47,625 --> 00:00:48,749
Probably your brothers.

22
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:51,082
Two mustard, please!
Thanks, Mama.

23
00:00:51,083 --> 00:00:51,917
Got it!

24
00:00:52,458 --> 00:00:54,000
Nate, mayo or mustard?

25
00:00:54,625 --> 00:00:55,833
How about ketchup?

26
00:00:56,375 --> 00:00:58,499
Or ketchup.
I got ketchup, too.

27
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,750
Mind your elbow.

28
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:03,666
Good job, hawk-eye.

29
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:06,583
Go get your arrow.

30
00:01:08,625 --> 00:01:09,707
Hey, guys!

31
00:01:09,708 --> 00:01:12,166
Enough practice. Soup's on!

32
00:01:12,167 --> 00:01:13,374
All right.

33
00:01:13,375 --> 00:01:14,750
We're coming. We're hungry.

34
00:01:15,625 --> 00:01:17,292
Lila, let's go.

35
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:21,583
Lila?

36
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,500
Honey?

37
00:01:29,375 --> 00:01:30,542
Hey, babe?

38
00:01:40,042 --> 00:01:41,417
Babe?

39
00:01:43,375 --> 00:01:44,667
Babe?

40
00:01:45,583 --> 00:01:47,542
Boys!

41
00:01:49,417 --> 00:01:50,250
Boys!

42
00:01:52,583 --> 00:01:53,832
Laura!

43
00:02:11,667 --> 00:02:17,541
<i>♪ Dear Mister Fantasy
Play us a tune ♪</i>

44
00:02:17,542 --> 00:02:22,125
<i>♪ Something
To make us all happy ♪</i>

45
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:28,916
<i>♪ Do anything take us out
of this gloom ♪</i>

46
00:02:28,917 --> 00:02:32,041
<i>♪ Sing a song, play guitar ♪</i>

47
00:02:32,042 --> 00:02:34,625
<i>♪ Make it snappy ♪</i>

48
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:38,792
You don't need to do that.

49
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:42,000
Because, uh, you're just
holding the position.

50
00:02:43,042 --> 00:02:44,374
Oh, yeah.

51
00:02:44,375 --> 00:02:45,541
That was close.

52
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:49,291
That's a goal.
We are now one apiece.

53
00:02:49,292 --> 00:02:50,667
I would like to try again.

54
00:02:53,125 --> 00:02:55,541
We're tied up.
Feel the tension?

55
00:02:55,542 --> 00:02:56,542
It's fun.

56
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:59,250
That was terrible.
Now you have a chance to win.

57
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:01,500
And you've won.

58
00:03:02,583 --> 00:03:03,916
Congratulations.

59
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:05,042
Fair game.

60
00:03:06,458 --> 00:03:07,750
Good sport.

61
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:10,125
You have fun?

62
00:03:11,958 --> 00:03:13,875
It was fun.

63
00:03:36,458 --> 00:03:38,000
This thing on?

64
00:03:40,167 --> 00:03:42,167
Hey, Miss Potts. Pep.

65
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:46,374
If you find this recording...

66
00:03:46,375 --> 00:03:49,207
don't post it on social media.

67
00:03:49,208 --> 00:03:50,917
It's gonna be
a real tearjerker.

68
00:03:51,583 --> 00:03:54,166
I don't know if
you're ever gonna see these.

69
00:03:54,167 --> 00:03:56,208
I don't even know
if you're still...

70
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:58,625
Oh, God, I hope so.

71
00:03:59,458 --> 00:04:01,874
<i>Today's day 21.</i>

72
00:04:01,875 --> 00:04:04,125
<i>No, uh, 22.</i>

73
00:04:04,792 --> 00:04:07,499
<i>You know, if it wasn't for
the existential terror</i>

74
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:09,666
<i>of staring into
the literal void of space,</i>

75
00:04:09,667 --> 00:04:12,124
<i>I'd say I'm feeling
a little better today.</i>

76
00:04:12,125 --> 00:04:13,624
<i>Infection's run its course,</i>

77
00:04:13,625 --> 00:04:15,167
<i>thanks to the Blue Meanie
back there.</i>

78
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:17,499
<i>Oh, you'd love her.</i>

79
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,917
<i>Very practical.</i>

80
00:04:19,417 --> 00:04:21,458
<i>Only a tiny bit sadistic.</i>

81
00:04:26,458 --> 00:04:28,707
<i>So, the fuel cells
were cracked during battle</i>

82
00:04:28,708 --> 00:04:31,041
<i>and we figured out a way
to reverse the ion charge</i>

83
00:04:31,042 --> 00:04:33,750
<i>and bought ourselves
about 48 hours of flight time.</i>

84
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:39,041
<i>Uh, but it's now dead
in the water.</i>

85
00:04:39,042 --> 00:04:42,542
<i>Thousand light years
from the nearest 7-Eleven.</i>

86
00:04:44,042 --> 00:04:46,417
<i>Oxygen will run out
tomorrow morning...</i>

87
00:04:47,917 --> 00:04:49,583
<i>and that'll be it.</i>

88
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:56,124
<i>Pep, I know I said
no more surprises,</i>

89
00:04:56,125 --> 00:04:57,916
<i>but I gotta say
I was really hoping</i>

90
00:04:57,917 --> 00:04:59,874
<i>to pull off one last one.</i>

91
00:04:59,875 --> 00:05:01,999
<i>But it looks like...</i>

92
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,792
<i>Well, you know
what it looks like.</i>

93
00:05:05,208 --> 00:05:07,207
Don't feel bad about this.

94
00:05:07,208 --> 00:05:10,000
I mean, actually, if
you grovel for a couple weeks,

95
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:13,875
and then move on
with enormous guilt...

96
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,041
I should probably lie down
for a minute.

97
00:05:21,042 --> 00:05:23,124
Go rest my eyes.

98
00:05:26,042 --> 00:05:27,583
Please know...

99
00:05:28,792 --> 00:05:32,582
when I drift off, it'll be
like every night lately.

100
00:05:32,583 --> 00:05:35,542
I'm fine. Totally fine.

101
00:05:36,208 --> 00:05:37,500
I dream about you.

102
00:05:39,083 --> 00:05:40,667
Because it's always you.

103
00:09:03,208 --> 00:09:04,332
Couldn't stop him.

104
00:09:04,333 --> 00:09:05,416
Neither could I.

105
00:09:05,417 --> 00:09:06,791
Hang on.

106
00:09:09,125 --> 00:09:10,708
I lost the kid.

107
00:09:13,250 --> 00:09:14,833
Tony, we lost.

108
00:09:17,125 --> 00:09:18,125
Is, uh...

109
00:09:19,125 --> 00:09:21,749
- Oh, good.
- Oh, my God!

110
00:09:21,750 --> 00:09:22,792
Oh, my God!

111
00:09:28,208 --> 00:09:29,917
It's okay.

112
00:09:36,292 --> 00:09:38,625
It's been 23 days
since Thanos came to Earth.

113
00:09:41,125 --> 00:09:43,707
World governments
are in pieces.

114
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:45,749
The parts that
are still working...

115
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:49,375
...are trying to take a census
and it looks like he did...

116
00:09:52,125 --> 00:09:53,749
He did exactly what he said
he was gonna do.

117
00:09:53,750 --> 00:09:55,000
Thanos wiped out...

118
00:09:57,583 --> 00:10:00,542
...50% of all
living creatures.

119
00:10:04,875 --> 00:10:06,957
Where is he now? Where?

120
00:10:06,958 --> 00:10:08,832
We don't know.

121
00:10:08,833 --> 00:10:11,917
He just opened a portal
and walked through.

122
00:10:14,542 --> 00:10:15,583
What's wrong with him?

123
00:10:16,667 --> 00:10:18,666
Oh, he's pissed.

124
00:10:18,667 --> 00:10:20,125
He thinks he failed.

125
00:10:21,583 --> 00:10:22,749
Which, of course, he did.

126
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:25,041
But there's a lot of that
going around, ain't there?

127
00:10:25,042 --> 00:10:26,707
Honestly,
until this exact second

128
00:10:26,708 --> 00:10:27,749
I thought
you were a Build-A-Bear.

129
00:10:27,750 --> 00:10:29,332
Maybe I am.

130
00:10:29,333 --> 00:10:30,874
We've been hunting Thanos
for three weeks now.

131
00:10:30,875 --> 00:10:33,124
Deep space scans and...

132
00:10:33,125 --> 00:10:35,083
satellites,
and we got nothing.

133
00:10:36,875 --> 00:10:38,041
Tony, you fought him.

134
00:10:38,042 --> 00:10:38,958
Who told you that?

135
00:10:39,625 --> 00:10:40,707
I didn't fight him.

136
00:10:40,708 --> 00:10:42,582
No, he wiped my face
with a planet

137
00:10:42,583 --> 00:10:45,166
while the Bleecker Street
magician gave away the store.

138
00:10:45,167 --> 00:10:46,416
That's what happened.
There was no fight,

139
00:10:46,417 --> 00:10:47,666
'cause he's not beatable.

140
00:10:47,667 --> 00:10:50,416
Did he give you any clues,
any coordinates, anything?

141
00:10:50,417 --> 00:10:51,917
Uh...

142
00:10:53,458 --> 00:10:55,041
I saw this coming
a few years back.

143
00:10:55,042 --> 00:10:56,667
I had a vision.
I didn't wanna believe it.

144
00:10:57,167 --> 00:10:58,791
Thought I was dreaming.

145
00:10:58,792 --> 00:10:59,957
Tony,
I'm gonna need you to focus.

146
00:10:59,958 --> 00:11:01,874
And I needed you.

147
00:11:01,875 --> 00:11:02,957
As in, past tense.

148
00:11:02,958 --> 00:11:06,374
That trumps what you need.
It's too late, buddy.

149
00:11:06,375 --> 00:11:07,625
Sorry.

150
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:11,292
You know what I need?
I need a shave.

151
00:11:11,958 --> 00:11:14,624
And I believe I remember
telling all youse...

152
00:11:14,625 --> 00:11:15,666
Tony, Tony!

153
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:17,166
...alive and otherwise,

154
00:11:17,167 --> 00:11:19,249
that what we needed

155
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:21,041
was a suit of armor
around the world.

156
00:11:21,042 --> 00:11:22,166
Remember that?

157
00:11:22,167 --> 00:11:24,916
Whether it impacted
our precious freedoms or not.

158
00:11:24,917 --> 00:11:26,291
That's what we needed.

159
00:11:26,292 --> 00:11:27,457
Well, that didn't
work out, did it?

160
00:11:27,458 --> 00:11:29,124
I said we'd lose.

161
00:11:29,125 --> 00:11:31,292
You said,
"We'll do that together, too."

162
00:11:31,833 --> 00:11:32,957
And guess what, Cap?

163
00:11:32,958 --> 00:11:34,375
We lost.

164
00:11:34,875 --> 00:11:35,833
And you weren't there.

165
00:11:37,417 --> 00:11:38,749
But that's what we do, right?

166
00:11:38,750 --> 00:11:41,666
Our best work after the fact?
We're the "Avengers."

167
00:11:41,667 --> 00:11:43,791
We're the "Avengers,"
not the "Pre-vengers."

168
00:11:43,792 --> 00:11:44,874
- Okay.
- Right?

169
00:11:44,875 --> 00:11:46,249
You made your point.
Just sit down, okay?

170
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:47,374
Okay. No, no, here's my point.
You know what?

171
00:11:47,375 --> 00:11:48,999
- She's great by the way.
- Tony, you're sick. Sit down.

172
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,791
We need you.
You're new blood.

173
00:11:50,792 --> 00:11:53,791
Bunch of tired old mules.
I got nothing for you, Cap.

174
00:11:53,792 --> 00:11:55,124
I got no coordinates,

175
00:11:55,125 --> 00:11:58,166
no clues,
no strategies, no options.

176
00:11:58,167 --> 00:12:00,041
Zero. Zip. Nada.

177
00:12:00,042 --> 00:12:01,792
No trust, liar.

178
00:12:06,333 --> 00:12:07,749
Here, take this.

179
00:12:07,750 --> 00:12:09,833
You find him, you put that on.

180
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:11,875
You hide.

181
00:12:13,167 --> 00:12:14,957
-  Tony!
- I'm fine.

182
00:12:14,958 --> 00:12:16,750
Let me...

183
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:24,582
Bruce gave him a sedative.

184
00:12:24,583 --> 00:12:26,417
He's gonna probably be out
for the rest of the day.

185
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:29,124
You guys take care of him

186
00:12:29,125 --> 00:12:30,667
and I'll bring him a Xorrian
elixir when I come back.

187
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:32,291
Where are you going?

188
00:12:32,292 --> 00:12:34,083
To kill Thanos.

189
00:12:37,125 --> 00:12:38,499
Hey.

190
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,332
You know, we usually
work as a team here,

191
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:42,541
and, between you and I,
morale's a little fragile.

192
00:12:42,542 --> 00:12:44,832
We realize up there
is more your territory,

193
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:46,207
but this is our fight, too.

194
00:12:46,208 --> 00:12:47,624
You even know where he is?

195
00:12:47,625 --> 00:12:48,874
I know people who might.

196
00:12:48,875 --> 00:12:50,292
Don't bother.

197
00:12:51,250 --> 00:12:53,000
I can tell you
where Thanos is.

198
00:12:55,542 --> 00:12:59,124
Thanos spent a long time
trying to perfect me.

199
00:12:59,125 --> 00:13:02,500
And when he worked, he talked
about his Great Plan.

200
00:13:03,333 --> 00:13:06,499
Even disassembled,
I wanted to please him.

201
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,000
I'd ask...

202
00:13:08,542 --> 00:13:11,208
where would we go
once his plan was complete?

203
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:13,708
And his answer
was always the same.

204
00:13:17,917 --> 00:13:18,917
"To the Garden."

205
00:13:19,583 --> 00:13:22,457
That's cute.
Thanos has a retirement plan.

206
00:13:22,458 --> 00:13:23,542
So, where is he?

207
00:13:24,292 --> 00:13:26,582
When Thanos
snapped his fingers,

208
00:13:26,583 --> 00:13:28,457
Earth became ground zero
for a power surge

209
00:13:28,458 --> 00:13:30,624
of ridiculously
cosmic proportions.

210
00:13:30,625 --> 00:13:32,333
No one's ever seen anything
like it.

211
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,333
Until two days ago...

212
00:13:36,167 --> 00:13:37,750
on this planet.

213
00:13:38,458 --> 00:13:39,958
Thanos is there.

214
00:13:41,667 --> 00:13:43,416
He used the stones again.

215
00:13:43,417 --> 00:13:44,958
Hey, hey, hey.

216
00:13:45,458 --> 00:13:47,582
We'd be going in
shorthanded, you know?

217
00:13:47,583 --> 00:13:49,124
Look, he's still
got the stones, so...

218
00:13:49,125 --> 00:13:50,832
So, let's get 'em.

219
00:13:50,833 --> 00:13:52,374
Use them to bring
everyone back.

220
00:13:52,375 --> 00:13:53,624
Just like that?

221
00:13:53,625 --> 00:13:55,374
Yeah. Just like that.

222
00:13:55,375 --> 00:13:58,707
Even if there's a small chance
that we can undo this,

223
00:13:58,708 --> 00:14:01,582
I mean, we owe it to everyone
who's not in this room to try.

224
00:14:01,583 --> 00:14:03,957
If we do this, how do
we know it's gonna end

225
00:14:03,958 --> 00:14:05,707
any differently
than it did before?

226
00:14:05,708 --> 00:14:07,333
Because before
you didn't have me.

227
00:14:08,208 --> 00:14:09,541
Hey, new girl?

228
00:14:09,542 --> 00:14:12,250
Everybody in this room
is about that superhero life.

229
00:14:13,042 --> 00:14:14,041
And if you don't mind
my asking,

230
00:14:14,042 --> 00:14:15,207
where the hell
have you been all this time?

231
00:14:15,208 --> 00:14:17,791
There are a lot of
other planets in the universe.

232
00:14:17,792 --> 00:14:20,667
And unfortunately,
they didn't have you guys.

233
00:14:40,292 --> 00:14:42,375
I like this one.

234
00:14:46,917 --> 00:14:49,500
Let's go get
this son of a bitch.

235
00:15:11,125 --> 00:15:12,125
Okay.

236
00:15:12,667 --> 00:15:14,917
Who here hasn't been to space?

237
00:15:16,292 --> 00:15:17,582
Why?

238
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:19,416
You better not throw up
on my ship.

239
00:15:19,417 --> 00:15:21,124
Approaching jump in three,

240
00:15:21,125 --> 00:15:22,958
two, one.

241
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:38,208
I'll head down for recon.

242
00:15:56,708 --> 00:15:57,917
This is gonna work, Steve.

243
00:15:58,458 --> 00:15:59,875
I know it will.

244
00:16:03,708 --> 00:16:06,000
'Cause I don't know what
I'm gonna do if it doesn't.

245
00:16:06,583 --> 00:16:10,249
<i>No satellites.
No ships. No armies.</i>

246
00:16:10,250 --> 00:16:11,750
<i>No ground defenses
of any kind.</i>

247
00:16:13,833 --> 00:16:15,500
<i>It's just him.</i>

248
00:16:16,125 --> 00:16:17,875
And that's enough.

249
00:17:47,042 --> 00:17:48,250
Oh, no.

250
00:17:58,125 --> 00:17:59,458
Where are they?

251
00:17:59,792 --> 00:18:01,292
Answer the question.

252
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:06,291
The universe
required correction.

253
00:18:06,292 --> 00:18:10,249
After that, the stones
served no purpose...

254
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:12,041
beyond temptation.

255
00:18:12,042 --> 00:18:14,000
You murdered trillions!

256
00:18:14,958 --> 00:18:17,292
You should be grateful.

257
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:22,832
Where are the stones?

258
00:18:22,833 --> 00:18:24,374
Gone.

259
00:18:24,375 --> 00:18:26,124
Reduced to atoms.

260
00:18:26,125 --> 00:18:27,791
You used them two days ago!

261
00:18:27,792 --> 00:18:31,000
I used the stones
to destroy the stones.

262
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:33,375
It nearly killed me.

263
00:18:34,792 --> 00:18:36,542
But the work is done.

264
00:18:36,958 --> 00:18:39,625
It always will be.

265
00:18:41,208 --> 00:18:44,583
I am inevitable.

266
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:49,416
We have to tear this place
apart. H-He has to be lying!

267
00:18:49,417 --> 00:18:53,583
My father is many things.
A liar is not one of them.

268
00:18:55,625 --> 00:18:58,917
Ah. Thank you, daughter.

269
00:19:01,792 --> 00:19:03,791
Perhaps I treated you
too harshly.

270
00:19:10,208 --> 00:19:11,208
What?

271
00:19:11,875 --> 00:19:13,625
What did you do?

272
00:19:15,167 --> 00:19:16,958
I went for the head.

273
00:20:27,792 --> 00:20:30,042
So I, uh...

274
00:20:31,292 --> 00:20:33,916
I went on a date
the other day.

275
00:20:33,917 --> 00:20:35,749
It's the first time
in five years.

276
00:20:35,750 --> 00:20:38,083
You know?
I'm sitting there at dinner.

277
00:20:38,750 --> 00:20:41,292
I... I didn't even know
what to talk about.

278
00:20:42,625 --> 00:20:43,916
What did you talk about?

279
00:20:43,917 --> 00:20:47,667
Eh, same old crap. You know,
how things have changed.

280
00:20:48,292 --> 00:20:49,917
My job, his job.

281
00:20:50,917 --> 00:20:52,792
How much we miss the Mets.

282
00:20:55,208 --> 00:20:56,750
And then things got quiet...

283
00:20:58,958 --> 00:21:02,624
then he cried as they were
serving the salads.

284
00:21:02,625 --> 00:21:04,125
What about you?

285
00:21:05,208 --> 00:21:08,458
I cried just before dessert.

286
00:21:12,208 --> 00:21:14,999
But I'm seeing him again
tomorrow, so...

287
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,416
That's great.

288
00:21:16,417 --> 00:21:18,166
You did the hardest part.
You took the jump.

289
00:21:18,167 --> 00:21:20,292
You didn't know where
you were gonna come down.

290
00:21:20,917 --> 00:21:22,874
And that's it.
That's those little

291
00:21:22,875 --> 00:21:25,374
brave baby steps
we gotta take...

292
00:21:25,375 --> 00:21:29,083
to try and become whole again,
try and find purpose.

293
00:21:30,917 --> 00:21:32,582
I went in the ice in '45,

294
00:21:32,583 --> 00:21:34,917
right after I met
the love of my life.

295
00:21:35,792 --> 00:21:37,542
Woke up 70 years later.

296
00:21:40,667 --> 00:21:42,708
You gotta move on.

297
00:21:45,417 --> 00:21:47,042
Gotta move on.

298
00:21:51,875 --> 00:21:54,457
The world is in our hands.

299
00:21:54,458 --> 00:21:56,707
It's left to us, guys.

300
00:21:56,708 --> 00:21:58,917
And we gotta do
something with it.

301
00:21:59,625 --> 00:22:01,042
Otherwise...

302
00:22:02,333 --> 00:22:04,667
Thanos should've killed
all of us.

303
00:23:06,542 --> 00:23:07,875
What the hell?

304
00:23:20,125 --> 00:23:21,500
Hope?

305
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:39,250
What?

306
00:23:54,667 --> 00:23:55,832
Kid!

307
00:23:55,833 --> 00:23:56,875
Hey, kid!

308
00:24:01,208 --> 00:24:03,417
What the hell happened here?

309
00:24:35,042 --> 00:24:36,833
Oh, my God!

310
00:24:39,667 --> 00:24:41,291
Oh, please!

311
00:24:41,292 --> 00:24:42,999
Please, please!

312
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:45,000
No, no, no. No.

313
00:24:46,458 --> 00:24:47,833
No.

314
00:24:50,167 --> 00:24:51,332
Excuse me. Sorry.

315
00:24:51,333 --> 00:24:52,791
Oh, Cassie, no.

316
00:24:52,792 --> 00:24:54,250
No, no, no.

317
00:24:55,625 --> 00:24:57,333
No, no.

318
00:24:58,250 --> 00:25:01,167
Please, please, please.
No, Cassie.

319
00:25:08,375 --> 00:25:09,542
What?

320
00:25:39,583 --> 00:25:40,917
Cassie?

321
00:25:42,083 --> 00:25:43,458
Dad?

322
00:26:09,458 --> 00:26:12,167
You're so big!

323
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:26,332
<i>Yeah. We boarded</i>

324
00:26:26,333 --> 00:26:29,832
<i>that highly-suspect warship
Danvers pinged.</i>

325
00:26:29,833 --> 00:26:31,791
<i>It was an infectious
garbage scow.</i>

326
00:26:31,792 --> 00:26:33,416
<i>So, thanks for the hot tip.</i>

327
00:26:33,417 --> 00:26:34,832
<i>Well, you were closer.</i>

328
00:26:34,833 --> 00:26:36,374
<i>Yeah.
And now we smell like garbage.</i>

329
00:26:36,375 --> 00:26:37,874
You get a reading
on those tremors?

330
00:26:37,875 --> 00:26:40,541
<i>Twas a mild subduction
under the African plate.</i>

331
00:26:40,542 --> 00:26:42,832
Do we have a visual?
How are we handling it?

332
00:26:42,833 --> 00:26:44,000
<i>Nat.</i>

333
00:26:44,375 --> 00:26:46,582
<i>It's an earthquake
under the ocean.</i>

334
00:26:46,583 --> 00:26:49,333
<i>We handle it
by not handling it.</i>

335
00:26:50,083 --> 00:26:52,208
Carol, are we seeing you here
next month?

336
00:26:52,667 --> 00:26:53,832
<i>Not likely.</i>

337
00:26:53,833 --> 00:26:55,541
<i>What? You gonna get
another haircut?</i>

338
00:26:55,542 --> 00:26:57,041
<i>Listen, fur face.</i>

339
00:26:57,042 --> 00:26:58,874
<i>I'm covering
a lot of territory.</i>

340
00:26:58,875 --> 00:27:00,832
<i>The things
that are happening on Earth</i>

341
00:27:00,833 --> 00:27:02,125
<i>are happening everywhere.</i>

342
00:27:02,458 --> 00:27:04,332
<i>On thousands of planets.</i>

343
00:27:04,333 --> 00:27:05,999
<i>All right, all right.
That's a good point.</i>

344
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,291
<i>That's a good point.</i>

345
00:27:07,292 --> 00:27:09,375
<i>So, you might not see me
for a long time.</i>

346
00:27:10,208 --> 00:27:11,875
All right. Uh, well...

347
00:27:12,750 --> 00:27:15,041
This channel's always active.

348
00:27:15,042 --> 00:27:17,291
So, if anything
goes sideways...

349
00:27:17,292 --> 00:27:19,874
anyone's making trouble
where they shouldn't...

350
00:27:19,875 --> 00:27:21,082
comes through me.

351
00:27:21,083 --> 00:27:22,832
<i>Okay.</i>

352
00:27:22,833 --> 00:27:24,292
All right.

353
00:27:25,042 --> 00:27:26,125
<i>Good luck.</i>

354
00:27:34,708 --> 00:27:36,916
- Where are you?
-  <i>Mexico.</i>

355
00:27:36,917 --> 00:27:39,832
<i>The Federales found
a room full of bodies.</i>

356
00:27:39,833 --> 00:27:41,624
<i>Looks like
a bunch of cartel guys...</i>

357
00:27:41,625 --> 00:27:43,624
<i>never even had a chance
to get their guns off.</i>

358
00:27:43,625 --> 00:27:45,624
It's probably a rival gang.

359
00:27:45,625 --> 00:27:46,874
<i>Except it isn't.</i>

360
00:27:46,875 --> 00:27:49,167
<i>It's definitely Barton.</i>

361
00:27:49,750 --> 00:27:51,416
<i>What he's done here...</i>

362
00:27:51,417 --> 00:27:54,667
<i>what he's been doing
for the last few years...</i>

363
00:27:55,500 --> 00:27:57,292
<i>I mean,
the scene that he left...</i>

364
00:27:58,292 --> 00:27:59,374
<i>I gotta tell you,</i>

365
00:27:59,375 --> 00:28:01,833
<i>there's a part of me that
doesn't even wanna find him.</i>

366
00:28:07,417 --> 00:28:09,667
Will you find out
where he's going next?

367
00:28:13,583 --> 00:28:14,708
<i>Nat?</i>

368
00:28:16,500 --> 00:28:18,208
Please?

369
00:28:19,958 --> 00:28:21,125
<i>Okay.</i>

370
00:28:29,917 --> 00:28:31,750
You know, I'd offer
to cook you dinner...

371
00:28:32,083 --> 00:28:33,667
but you seem
pretty miserable already.

372
00:28:37,750 --> 00:28:39,332
You here to do your laundry?

373
00:28:39,333 --> 00:28:40,917
And to see a friend.

374
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:44,667
Clearly, your friend is fine.

375
00:28:47,417 --> 00:28:48,874
You know,
I saw a pod of whales

376
00:28:48,875 --> 00:28:50,082
when I was coming over
the bridge.

377
00:28:50,083 --> 00:28:52,082
- In the Hudson?
- There's fewer ships...

378
00:28:52,083 --> 00:28:53,499
cleaner water.

379
00:28:53,500 --> 00:28:55,249
You know,
if you're about to tell me

380
00:28:55,250 --> 00:28:58,458
to look on
the bright side, um...

381
00:28:59,792 --> 00:29:01,249
I'm about to hit you
in the head,

382
00:29:01,250 --> 00:29:03,416
with a peanut butter sandwich.

383
00:29:03,417 --> 00:29:04,417
Hmm.

384
00:29:05,333 --> 00:29:06,666
Sorry.

385
00:29:06,667 --> 00:29:07,833
Force of habit.

386
00:29:22,083 --> 00:29:23,541
You know,
I keep telling everybody

387
00:29:23,542 --> 00:29:25,208
they should move on...

388
00:29:25,542 --> 00:29:27,042
and grow.

389
00:29:28,250 --> 00:29:29,542
Some do.

390
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,500
But not us.

391
00:29:35,250 --> 00:29:37,292
If I move on, who does this?

392
00:29:37,667 --> 00:29:39,792
Maybe it doesn't
need to be done.

393
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:46,250
I used to have nothing.

394
00:29:47,250 --> 00:29:49,333
And then I got this.

395
00:29:51,500 --> 00:29:53,333
This job.

396
00:29:55,708 --> 00:29:57,458
This family.

397
00:30:01,250 --> 00:30:05,125
And I was...
I was better because of it.

398
00:30:11,375 --> 00:30:14,917
And even though
they're gone...

399
00:30:18,875 --> 00:30:21,292
I'm still trying to be better.

400
00:30:24,333 --> 00:30:26,750
I think we both need
to get a life.

401
00:30:29,167 --> 00:30:30,583
You first.

402
00:30:36,125 --> 00:30:38,749
<i>Oh, hi, hi!
Uh, is anyone home?</i>

403
00:30:38,750 --> 00:30:40,624
<i>This is, uh, Scott Lang.</i>

404
00:30:40,625 --> 00:30:43,624
<i>We met a few years ago
at the airport...</i>

405
00:30:43,625 --> 00:30:45,457
<i>in Germany?</i>

406
00:30:45,458 --> 00:30:47,916
<i>I was the guy that got
really big. I had a mask on.</i>

407
00:30:47,917 --> 00:30:49,582
- <i>You wouldn't recognize me.</i>
- Is this an old message?

408
00:30:49,583 --> 00:30:52,707
<i>Ant-Man?
I know you know that.</i>

409
00:30:52,708 --> 00:30:53,874
It's the front gate.

410
00:30:53,875 --> 00:30:55,332
<i>I really need to
talk to you guys.</i>

411
00:31:01,458 --> 00:31:02,625
Scott.

412
00:31:03,542 --> 00:31:04,624
Are you okay?

413
00:31:04,625 --> 00:31:05,750
Yeah.

414
00:31:07,542 --> 00:31:09,917
Have either of you guys
ever studied quantum physics?

415
00:31:10,333 --> 00:31:11,833
Only to make conversation.

416
00:31:12,917 --> 00:31:14,542
All right, so...

417
00:31:14,917 --> 00:31:17,625
five years ago,
right... right before...

418
00:31:18,208 --> 00:31:19,333
Thanos...

419
00:31:19,708 --> 00:31:21,957
I was in a place called
the quantum realm.

420
00:31:21,958 --> 00:31:24,499
The quantum realm is like
its own microscopic universe.

421
00:31:24,500 --> 00:31:26,916
To get in there, you have
to be incredibly small.

422
00:31:26,917 --> 00:31:28,458
Hope. She's my, um...

423
00:31:30,542 --> 00:31:32,250
She w-was my...

424
00:31:33,958 --> 00:31:35,332
She was supposed to
pull me out.

425
00:31:35,333 --> 00:31:37,082
And then Thanos happened...

426
00:31:37,083 --> 00:31:38,750
and I got stuck in there.

427
00:31:39,208 --> 00:31:41,332
I'm sorry, that must have been
a very long five years.

428
00:31:41,333 --> 00:31:42,749
Yeah, but that's just it.

429
00:31:42,750 --> 00:31:44,166
It wasn't.

430
00:31:44,167 --> 00:31:45,541
For me, it was five hours.

431
00:31:45,542 --> 00:31:46,999
See, the rules
of the quantum realm

432
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:48,124
aren't like they are up here.

433
00:31:48,125 --> 00:31:49,832
Everything is unpredictable.

434
00:31:49,833 --> 00:31:51,082
Is that anybody's sandwich?

435
00:31:51,083 --> 00:31:52,458
I'm starving.

436
00:31:52,792 --> 00:31:54,082
Scott.

437
00:31:54,083 --> 00:31:55,375
What are you talking about?

438
00:31:56,375 --> 00:31:57,625
So...

439
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:00,167
what I'm saying is...

440
00:32:01,042 --> 00:32:03,624
time works differently
in the quantum realm.

441
00:32:03,625 --> 00:32:05,582
The only problem is right now

442
00:32:05,583 --> 00:32:07,082
we don't have
a way to navigate it.

443
00:32:07,083 --> 00:32:08,083
But what if we did?

444
00:32:08,833 --> 00:32:10,082
I can't stop
thinking about it.

445
00:32:10,083 --> 00:32:12,207
What if we could somehow
control the chaos...

446
00:32:12,208 --> 00:32:13,499
and we could navigate it?

447
00:32:13,500 --> 00:32:15,166
What if there was a way...

448
00:32:15,167 --> 00:32:16,874
that we could enter
the quantum realm

449
00:32:16,875 --> 00:32:18,124
at a certain point in time...

450
00:32:18,125 --> 00:32:19,582
but then exit
the quantum realm

451
00:32:19,583 --> 00:32:20,999
at another point in time?

452
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:22,333
Like...

453
00:32:23,083 --> 00:32:25,207
- Like before Thanos.
-  Wait.

454
00:32:25,208 --> 00:32:27,082
Are you talking about
a time machine?

455
00:32:27,083 --> 00:32:29,999
No. No, of course not.
No, not a time machine.

456
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:31,042
This is more like a...

457
00:32:33,250 --> 00:32:35,082
Yeah. Like a time machine.

458
00:32:35,083 --> 00:32:37,041
I know, it's crazy.
It's crazy.

459
00:32:37,042 --> 00:32:39,249
But I can't stop
thinking about it.

460
00:32:39,250 --> 00:32:40,500
There's gotta be...

461
00:32:41,250 --> 00:32:42,707
some way...

462
00:32:42,708 --> 00:32:44,666
- It's crazy.
-  Scott.

463
00:32:44,667 --> 00:32:46,124
I get emails from a raccoon...

464
00:32:46,125 --> 00:32:48,125
so nothing sounds crazy
anymore.

465
00:32:48,875 --> 00:32:50,958
So, who do we talk to
about this?

466
00:33:09,042 --> 00:33:10,125
Chow time!

467
00:33:12,583 --> 00:33:13,625
Maguna.

468
00:33:18,042 --> 00:33:19,417
Morgan H. Stark,
you want some lunch?

469
00:33:20,417 --> 00:33:21,417
<i>Define "lunch"</i>

470
00:33:21,542 --> 00:33:22,792
<i>- or be disintegrated.</i>
- Okay.

471
00:33:24,167 --> 00:33:25,791
You should not
be wearing that, okay?

472
00:33:25,792 --> 00:33:27,332
That is part of
a special anniversary gift

473
00:33:27,333 --> 00:33:28,333
I'm making for Mom.

474
00:33:32,083 --> 00:33:34,832
There you go.
You thinking about lunch?

475
00:33:34,833 --> 00:33:36,916
I can give you a handful of
crickets on a bed of lettuce.

476
00:33:36,917 --> 00:33:38,666
- No.
- That's what you want.

477
00:33:38,667 --> 00:33:41,082
How did you find this?

478
00:33:41,083 --> 00:33:43,082
- Garage.
- Really?

479
00:33:43,083 --> 00:33:45,083
- Were you looking for it?
- No.

480
00:33:45,958 --> 00:33:47,999
- I found it, though.
- Hmm.

481
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:49,916
You like going
in the garage, huh?

482
00:33:49,917 --> 00:33:51,167
So does Daddy.

483
00:33:51,917 --> 00:33:54,750
It's fine, actually. Mom never
wears anything I buy her.

484
00:33:57,458 --> 00:33:58,708
So, I'm gonna...

485
00:34:16,208 --> 00:34:18,832
No. We know
what it sounds like.

486
00:34:18,833 --> 00:34:19,957
Tony, after everything
you've seen,

487
00:34:19,958 --> 00:34:20,999
is anything really impossible?

488
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,416
Quantum fluctuation messes
with the Planck Scale...

489
00:34:23,417 --> 00:34:24,917
which then triggers the
Deutsch Proposition.

490
00:34:25,042 --> 00:34:26,249
Can we agree on that?

491
00:34:26,250 --> 00:34:27,499
Thank you.

492
00:34:27,500 --> 00:34:29,791
In layman's terms, it
means you're not coming home.

493
00:34:29,792 --> 00:34:31,499
- I did.
- No.

494
00:34:31,500 --> 00:34:32,917
You accidentally survived.

495
00:34:33,458 --> 00:34:35,791
It's a billion-to-one
cosmic fluke.

496
00:34:35,792 --> 00:34:38,875
And now you wanna pull a...
What do you call it?

497
00:34:40,917 --> 00:34:42,416
A time heist?

498
00:34:42,417 --> 00:34:44,541
Yeah, a time heist. Of course.

499
00:34:44,542 --> 00:34:45,916
Why didn't we
think of this before?

500
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:48,541
Oh, because it's laughable.
Because it's a pipe dream.

501
00:34:48,542 --> 00:34:50,416
The stones are in the past.

502
00:34:50,417 --> 00:34:52,166
We could go back,
we could get them.

503
00:34:52,167 --> 00:34:54,749
We can snap our own fingers.
We can bring everybody back.

504
00:34:54,750 --> 00:34:56,832
Or screw it up worse
than he already has, right?

505
00:34:56,833 --> 00:34:57,833
I don't believe we would.

506
00:34:58,417 --> 00:35:00,958
Gotta say it. I sometimes
miss that giddy optimism.

507
00:35:01,833 --> 00:35:03,707
However, high hopes
won't help...

508
00:35:03,708 --> 00:35:05,832
if there's no logical,
tangible way for me

509
00:35:05,833 --> 00:35:09,249
to safely execute
said time heist.

510
00:35:09,250 --> 00:35:10,874
I believe the most
likely outcome

511
00:35:10,875 --> 00:35:12,332
will be our collective demise.

512
00:35:12,333 --> 00:35:15,416
Not if we strictly follow
the rules of time travel.

513
00:35:15,417 --> 00:35:18,166
All right? It means no talking
to our past selves...

514
00:35:18,167 --> 00:35:19,874
no betting on sporting events.

515
00:35:19,875 --> 00:35:21,625
I'm gonna stop you
right there, Scott.

516
00:35:22,542 --> 00:35:23,999
Are you seriously telling me

517
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:25,957
that your plan
to save the universe...

518
00:35:25,958 --> 00:35:27,707
is based on
<i>Back to the Future?</i>

519
00:35:28,792 --> 00:35:30,541
- Is it?
- No.

520
00:35:30,542 --> 00:35:31,749
Good.
You had me worried there.

521
00:35:31,750 --> 00:35:32,874
'Cause that
would be horseshit.

522
00:35:32,875 --> 00:35:35,457
That's not how
quantum physics works.

523
00:35:35,458 --> 00:35:36,625
Tony.

524
00:35:38,583 --> 00:35:40,042
We have to take a stand.

525
00:35:40,708 --> 00:35:42,583
We did stand.
And yet, here we are.

526
00:35:44,917 --> 00:35:46,208
I know you got
a lot on the line.

527
00:35:46,708 --> 00:35:49,416
You got a wife, a daughter.

528
00:35:49,417 --> 00:35:52,082
But I lost someone
very important to me.

529
00:35:52,083 --> 00:35:53,832
A lotta people did.

530
00:35:53,833 --> 00:35:56,999
And now, now we have a chance
to bring her back...

531
00:35:57,000 --> 00:35:58,207
to bring everyone back,

532
00:35:58,208 --> 00:35:59,832
and you're telling me
that you won't even...

533
00:35:59,833 --> 00:36:01,625
That's right, Scott.
I won't even.

534
00:36:03,333 --> 00:36:04,707
I can't.

535
00:36:06,583 --> 00:36:09,249
Mommy told
me to come and save you.

536
00:36:09,250 --> 00:36:11,667
Good job. I'm saved.

537
00:36:12,417 --> 00:36:14,541
I wish you were coming here
to ask me something else.

538
00:36:14,542 --> 00:36:15,749
Anything else.

539
00:36:15,750 --> 00:36:17,707
I'm honestly happy
to see you guys, I just...

540
00:36:17,708 --> 00:36:18,791
Oh, look, the table's
set for six.

541
00:36:18,792 --> 00:36:20,749
Tony. I get it.

542
00:36:20,750 --> 00:36:23,042
And I'm happy for you.
I really am.

543
00:36:23,833 --> 00:36:25,333
But this is a second chance.

544
00:36:26,042 --> 00:36:28,624
I got my second chance
right here, Cap.

545
00:36:28,625 --> 00:36:30,167
Can't roll the dice on it.

546
00:36:32,250 --> 00:36:34,167
If you don't talk shop,
you can stay for lunch.

547
00:36:37,417 --> 00:36:38,625
Well, he's scared.

548
00:36:39,292 --> 00:36:40,499
He's not wrong.

549
00:36:40,500 --> 00:36:42,666
Yeah, but, I mean,
what are we gonna do?

550
00:36:42,667 --> 00:36:43,958
We need him.
What, are we gonna stop?

551
00:36:44,875 --> 00:36:46,875
No, I wanna do it right.

552
00:36:50,083 --> 00:36:51,750
We're gonna need
a really big brain.

553
00:36:52,833 --> 00:36:54,250
Bigger than his?

554
00:36:54,708 --> 00:36:56,374
Come on, I feel like I'm
the only one eating here.

555
00:36:56,375 --> 00:36:57,499
Try some of that.

556
00:36:57,500 --> 00:36:58,500
Have some eggs.

557
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:00,416
I'm so confused.

558
00:37:00,417 --> 00:37:02,249
These are confusing times.

559
00:37:02,250 --> 00:37:04,332
Right, no, no.
That's not what I meant.

560
00:37:04,333 --> 00:37:06,833
Nah, I get it. I'm kidding!

561
00:37:07,417 --> 00:37:09,374
I know, it's crazy.

562
00:37:09,375 --> 00:37:10,624
I'm wearing shirts now.

563
00:37:10,625 --> 00:37:13,583
Yeah. What? How? Why?

564
00:37:14,042 --> 00:37:16,375
Five years ago,
we got our asses beat.

565
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:18,791
Except it was worse for me...

566
00:37:18,792 --> 00:37:20,166
cause I lost twice.

567
00:37:20,167 --> 00:37:21,958
First, Hulk lost,
then Banner lost...

568
00:37:22,833 --> 00:37:24,249
and then, we all lost.

569
00:37:24,250 --> 00:37:25,541
No one blamed you, Bruce.

570
00:37:25,542 --> 00:37:27,042
I did.

571
00:37:28,792 --> 00:37:30,082
For years, I've been
treating the Hulk

572
00:37:30,083 --> 00:37:31,332
like he's some kind
of disease...

573
00:37:31,333 --> 00:37:32,792
something to get rid of.

574
00:37:33,542 --> 00:37:36,208
But then, I start
looking at him as the cure.

575
00:37:36,792 --> 00:37:39,082
Eighteen months
in the gamma lab.

576
00:37:39,083 --> 00:37:41,832
I put the brains
and the brawn together...

577
00:37:41,833 --> 00:37:43,083
and now, look at me.

578
00:37:44,125 --> 00:37:45,458
Best of both worlds.

579
00:37:46,208 --> 00:37:47,582
- Excuse me, Mr. Hulk?
- Yes.

580
00:37:47,583 --> 00:37:49,042
Can we get a photo?

581
00:37:49,458 --> 00:37:51,624
100%, little person.

582
00:37:51,625 --> 00:37:53,667
Come on, step on up.
Do you mind?

583
00:37:54,375 --> 00:37:56,207
- Oh, yeah, yeah.
- Thanks.

584
00:37:56,208 --> 00:37:57,957
Say "green."

585
00:37:57,958 --> 00:38:00,374
-  Green.
- Green.

586
00:38:00,375 --> 00:38:01,332
Did you get that?

587
00:38:01,333 --> 00:38:02,708
That's a good one.

588
00:38:03,500 --> 00:38:05,750
Did you want to grab one
with me? I'm Ant-Man.

589
00:38:09,417 --> 00:38:11,499
They're Hulk fans.
They don't know Ant-Man.

590
00:38:11,500 --> 00:38:12,624
Nobody does.

591
00:38:12,625 --> 00:38:13,666
He wants you to take
a picture with him

592
00:38:13,667 --> 00:38:15,624
- I don't want a picture.
-  Stranger danger.

593
00:38:15,625 --> 00:38:17,666
Yeah, look, he's even saying
no, he doesn't. I get it.

594
00:38:17,667 --> 00:38:19,541
- I don't want it, either.
- But come on. The kid...

595
00:38:19,542 --> 00:38:21,124
I don't want a picture
with them.

596
00:38:21,125 --> 00:38:22,291
- He's gonna feel bad.
- Sorry.

597
00:38:22,292 --> 00:38:23,624
They're happy to do it.
They said they'll do it.

598
00:38:23,625 --> 00:38:25,249
- I don't want to do it.
- We can do it.

599
00:38:25,250 --> 00:38:27,374
- No, you feel bad.
- Take the goddamn phone.

600
00:38:27,375 --> 00:38:28,624
Okay.

601
00:38:28,625 --> 00:38:30,416
- Thank you, Mr. Hulk.
- It was great, kids.

602
00:38:30,417 --> 00:38:31,417
Thank you very much.

603
00:38:31,875 --> 00:38:33,416
Hulk out!

604
00:38:33,417 --> 00:38:34,292
Bruce.

605
00:38:34,875 --> 00:38:35,875
Dab.

606
00:38:36,208 --> 00:38:37,833
- Bruce.
- Listen to your mom.

607
00:38:38,208 --> 00:38:39,249
She knows better.

608
00:38:39,250 --> 00:38:41,207
About what we were saying.

609
00:38:41,208 --> 00:38:42,417
Right.

610
00:38:44,375 --> 00:38:47,042
The whole time travel do-over?

611
00:38:48,333 --> 00:38:52,083
Eh, guys, it's outside
of my area of expertise.

612
00:38:52,542 --> 00:38:53,792
Well, you pulled this off.

613
00:38:54,833 --> 00:38:58,625
I remember a time when that
seemed pretty impossible, too.

614
00:39:31,875 --> 00:39:33,541
I've got a mild inspiration.

615
00:39:33,542 --> 00:39:34,874
I'd like to see
if it checks out.

616
00:39:34,875 --> 00:39:37,041
So, I'd like to run
one last sim

617
00:39:37,042 --> 00:39:38,791
before we pack it in
for the night.

618
00:39:38,792 --> 00:39:41,874
This time, in the shape of a
Mobius strip,

619
00:39:41,875 --> 00:39:43,332
inverted, please.

620
00:39:43,333 --> 00:39:44,417
<i>Processing.</i>

621
00:39:47,875 --> 00:39:50,541
Right, give me the eigenvalue
of that particle...

622
00:39:50,542 --> 00:39:52,707
factoring in spectral decomp.

623
00:39:52,708 --> 00:39:54,667
- That'll take a second.
- <i>Just a moment.</i>

624
00:39:55,708 --> 00:39:58,583
And don't worry if it doesn't
pan out. I'm just kinda...

625
00:40:00,125 --> 00:40:01,707
<i>Model rendered.</i>

626
00:40:13,417 --> 00:40:14,250
Shit!

627
00:40:14,750 --> 00:40:15,625
Shit!

628
00:40:20,042 --> 00:40:21,791
What are you
doing up, little miss?

629
00:40:21,792 --> 00:40:23,791
- Shit.
- Nope. We don't say that.

630
00:40:23,792 --> 00:40:25,166
Only Mommy says that word.

631
00:40:25,167 --> 00:40:26,749
She coined it.
It belongs to her.

632
00:40:26,750 --> 00:40:27,874
Why are you up?

633
00:40:27,875 --> 00:40:29,291
Cause I've got some important
shit going on here!

634
00:40:29,292 --> 00:40:30,749
Why do you think?

635
00:40:30,750 --> 00:40:32,207
No, I got something
on my mind.

636
00:40:32,208 --> 00:40:33,874
I got something on my mind.

637
00:40:33,875 --> 00:40:35,417
Was it juice pops?

638
00:40:36,958 --> 00:40:38,167
Sure was.

639
00:40:39,583 --> 00:40:41,499
That's extortion.
That's a word.

640
00:40:41,500 --> 00:40:42,832
What kind you want?

641
00:40:42,833 --> 00:40:43,999
Great minds think alike.

642
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,833
Juice pops exactly...

643
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:49,125
was on my mind.

644
00:40:50,542 --> 00:40:51,667
You done? Yeah?

645
00:40:52,208 --> 00:40:53,417
Now you are.

646
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:55,167
Here. Wipe.

647
00:40:57,875 --> 00:41:00,707
Good. That face goes there.

648
00:41:00,708 --> 00:41:02,124
Tell me a story.

649
00:41:02,125 --> 00:41:03,874
A story.

650
00:41:03,875 --> 00:41:06,000
Once upon a time, Maguna
went to bed. The end.

651
00:41:06,375 --> 00:41:07,916
That is a horrible story.

652
00:41:07,917 --> 00:41:09,667
Come on,
that's your favorite story.

653
00:41:10,375 --> 00:41:11,542
Love you tons.

654
00:41:13,542 --> 00:41:15,375
I love you 3,000.

655
00:41:16,625 --> 00:41:17,625
Wow.

656
00:41:24,958 --> 00:41:27,833
3,000. That's crazy.

657
00:41:29,042 --> 00:41:30,833
Go to bed
or I'll sell all your toys.

658
00:41:32,042 --> 00:41:33,416
Night night.

659
00:41:33,417 --> 00:41:34,750
Not that it's a competition...

660
00:41:35,250 --> 00:41:37,207
but she loves me 3,000.

661
00:41:37,208 --> 00:41:38,582
Does she, now?

662
00:41:38,583 --> 00:41:41,707
You were somewhere in
the low 6 to 900 range.

663
00:41:47,667 --> 00:41:49,167
Whatcha reading?

664
00:41:49,792 --> 00:41:51,291
Just a book on composting.

665
00:41:51,292 --> 00:41:53,500
What's new with composting?

666
00:41:54,958 --> 00:41:57,000
- Interesting science...
- I figured it out.

667
00:41:58,083 --> 00:41:59,083
By the way.

668
00:41:59,958 --> 00:42:01,832
And, you know, just so
we're talking

669
00:42:01,833 --> 00:42:03,499
about the same thing...

670
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:04,958
Time travel.

671
00:42:05,625 --> 00:42:06,458
What?

672
00:42:10,667 --> 00:42:11,667
Wow.

673
00:42:15,750 --> 00:42:17,292
That's amazing...

674
00:42:18,250 --> 00:42:19,541
and terrifying.

675
00:42:19,542 --> 00:42:21,000
That's right.

676
00:42:28,292 --> 00:42:30,166
We got really lucky.

677
00:42:30,167 --> 00:42:31,332
Yeah.

678
00:42:31,333 --> 00:42:32,499
I know.

679
00:42:32,500 --> 00:42:33,916
A lot of people didn't.

680
00:42:33,917 --> 00:42:35,542
Nope.
And I can't help everybody.

681
00:42:37,292 --> 00:42:38,666
Sorta seems like you can.

682
00:42:38,667 --> 00:42:40,417
Not if I stop.

683
00:42:41,583 --> 00:42:44,458
I can put a pin in it
right now and stop.

684
00:42:45,250 --> 00:42:46,250
Tony...

685
00:42:46,958 --> 00:42:48,666
trying to get you to stop...

686
00:42:48,667 --> 00:42:51,292
has been one of the few
failures of my entire life.

687
00:42:55,583 --> 00:42:57,250
Something tells me...

688
00:42:58,542 --> 00:42:59,999
I should put it in a lockbox
and drop it to the

689
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:01,208
bottom of the lake...

690
00:43:02,417 --> 00:43:03,625
and go to bed.

691
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:12,042
But would you be able to rest?

692
00:43:16,750 --> 00:43:20,249
<i>Okay, here we go.
Time travel test number one.</i>

693
00:43:20,250 --> 00:43:22,417
Scott, fire up...

694
00:43:23,333 --> 00:43:24,500
the, uh, van thing.

695
00:43:26,792 --> 00:43:27,874
Breakers are set.

696
00:43:27,875 --> 00:43:29,999
Emergency generators
are on standby.

697
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:31,624
Good,
because if we blow the grid,

698
00:43:31,625 --> 00:43:35,082
I don't want to lose, uh,
Tiny here in the 1950s.

699
00:43:35,083 --> 00:43:35,999
Excuse me?

700
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:38,207
He's kidding.

701
00:43:38,208 --> 00:43:40,332
You can't say
things like that.

702
00:43:40,333 --> 00:43:41,833
It was a bad joke.

703
00:43:43,833 --> 00:43:44,832
You were kidding, right?

704
00:43:44,833 --> 00:43:48,249
I have no idea. We're talking
about time travel here.

705
00:43:48,250 --> 00:43:50,666
Either it's all a joke,
or none of it is.

706
00:43:50,667 --> 00:43:52,499
We're good!

707
00:43:52,500 --> 00:43:53,833
Get your helmet on.

708
00:43:54,458 --> 00:43:56,416
Scott, I'm gonna send
you back a week...

709
00:43:56,417 --> 00:43:57,999
let you walk around
for an hour,

710
00:43:58,000 --> 00:43:59,791
then bring you back
in 10 seconds.

711
00:43:59,792 --> 00:44:00,792
Make sense?

712
00:44:01,458 --> 00:44:02,874
Perfectly not confusing.

713
00:44:02,875 --> 00:44:04,833
Good luck, Scott.
You got this.

714
00:44:06,375 --> 00:44:09,625
You're right.
I do, Captain America.

715
00:44:11,583 --> 00:44:13,082
On a count of three...

716
00:44:13,083 --> 00:44:16,999
Three, two, one.

717
00:44:20,208 --> 00:44:21,875
Uh... Guys?

718
00:44:22,417 --> 00:44:24,374
This doesn't feel right.

719
00:44:24,375 --> 00:44:25,374
What is this?

720
00:44:25,375 --> 00:44:26,291
- What's going on?
-  Who is that?

721
00:44:26,292 --> 00:44:27,249
- Hold on.
- Is that Scott?

722
00:44:27,250 --> 00:44:28,250
Yes, it's Scott.

723
00:44:29,208 --> 00:44:30,292
Hold on a second.

724
00:44:31,125 --> 00:44:33,832
- What's going on, Bruce?
- Oh, my back!

725
00:44:33,833 --> 00:44:34,957
- What is this?
- Hold on a second.

726
00:44:34,958 --> 00:44:35,999
Could I get a
little space here?

727
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:37,291
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Can you bring him back?

728
00:44:37,292 --> 00:44:38,583
I'm working on it.

729
00:44:45,292 --> 00:44:46,332
It's a baby.

730
00:44:46,333 --> 00:44:48,166
- It's Scott.
-  As a baby.

731
00:44:48,167 --> 00:44:49,707
- He'll grow.
- Bring Scott back.

732
00:44:49,708 --> 00:44:51,249
When I say kill the power,
kill the power.

733
00:44:51,250 --> 00:44:52,500
Oh, my God.

734
00:44:53,208 --> 00:44:54,583
And... kill it!

735
00:44:59,000 --> 00:45:00,832
Somebody peed my pants.

736
00:45:00,833 --> 00:45:01,957
Oh, thank God.

737
00:45:01,958 --> 00:45:05,292
But I don't know
if it was baby me or old me.

738
00:45:08,625 --> 00:45:10,583
Or just me me.

739
00:45:11,000 --> 00:45:12,208
Time travel!

740
00:45:15,958 --> 00:45:16,958
What?

741
00:45:18,625 --> 00:45:20,875
I see this as an absolute win.

742
00:46:06,500 --> 00:46:07,957
Why the long face?

743
00:46:07,958 --> 00:46:09,708
Let me guess,
he turned into a baby.

744
00:46:10,958 --> 00:46:13,124
Among other things, yeah.
What are you doing here?

745
00:46:13,125 --> 00:46:14,542
It's the EPR Paradox.

746
00:46:15,333 --> 00:46:16,416
Instead of pushing
Lang through

747
00:46:16,417 --> 00:46:19,124
time, you might've wound up...
pushing time through Lang.

748
00:46:19,125 --> 00:46:20,332
It's tricky, dangerous.

749
00:46:20,333 --> 00:46:21,957
Somebody could have
cautioned you against it.

750
00:46:21,958 --> 00:46:23,082
You did.

751
00:46:23,083 --> 00:46:24,457
Oh, did I?

752
00:46:24,458 --> 00:46:26,125
Well, thank God I'm here.

753
00:46:26,917 --> 00:46:28,542
Regardless, I fixed it.

754
00:46:29,625 --> 00:46:31,917
A fully functioning
time-space GPS.

755
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:35,250
I just want peace.

756
00:46:36,875 --> 00:46:39,583
Turns out resentment
is corrosive, and I hate it.

757
00:46:40,458 --> 00:46:41,833
Me, too.

758
00:46:43,083 --> 00:46:44,957
We got a shot at getting
these stones,

759
00:46:44,958 --> 00:46:46,707
but I gotta tell you
my priorities.

760
00:46:46,708 --> 00:46:49,207
Bring back what we lost,
I hope, yes.

761
00:46:49,208 --> 00:46:52,042
Keep what I found,
I have to, at all costs.

762
00:46:53,292 --> 00:46:56,041
And maybe not die trying.

763
00:46:56,042 --> 00:46:57,083
Would be nice.

764
00:46:59,542 --> 00:47:00,625
Sounds like a deal.

765
00:47:24,208 --> 00:47:25,249
Tony, I don't know.

766
00:47:25,250 --> 00:47:27,166
Why?

767
00:47:27,167 --> 00:47:29,124
He made it for you.

768
00:47:29,125 --> 00:47:30,999
Plus, I have to get it
out of the garage

769
00:47:31,000 --> 00:47:32,708
before Morgan
takes it sledding.

770
00:47:38,250 --> 00:47:39,375
Thank you, Tony.

771
00:47:40,375 --> 00:47:41,917
Will you keep that
a little quiet?

772
00:47:42,625 --> 00:47:44,000
Didn't bring one
for the whole team.

773
00:47:45,750 --> 00:47:49,207
We are getting
the whole team, yeah?

774
00:47:49,208 --> 00:47:50,958
We're working on
that right now.

775
00:48:09,042 --> 00:48:10,083
Hey, Humie.

776
00:48:10,625 --> 00:48:12,417
Where's Big Green?

777
00:48:12,750 --> 00:48:14,792
The kitchen, I think.

778
00:48:16,042 --> 00:48:17,250
That's awesome.

779
00:48:18,458 --> 00:48:20,707
Rhodey, careful on re-entry.

780
00:48:20,708 --> 00:48:22,417
There's an idiot
in the landing zone.

781
00:48:23,583 --> 00:48:24,708
Oh, God.

782
00:48:25,292 --> 00:48:27,333
What's up, Regular-Sized Man?

783
00:48:44,917 --> 00:48:47,416
<i>♪ Let me take you
On a little trip ♪</i>

784
00:48:47,417 --> 00:48:50,041
<i>♪ My supersonic ship's
At your disposal ♪</i>

785
00:48:50,042 --> 00:48:51,708
<i>♪ If you feel so inclined ♪</i>

786
00:48:53,875 --> 00:48:54,958
{\an8}<i>♪ Well all right ♪</i>

787
00:48:57,917 --> 00:49:00,291
{\an8}<i>♪ We're gonna travel
