What I want
you can't give me.

897
00:56:31,250 --> 00:56:32,375
You shouldn't be here.

898
00:56:35,167 --> 00:56:36,292
Neither should you.

899
00:56:42,833 --> 00:56:44,417
I've got a job to do.

900
00:56:46,042 --> 00:56:47,583
Is that
what you're calling this?

901
00:56:48,583 --> 00:56:51,000
Killing all these people isn't
gonna bring your family back.

902
00:56:56,792 --> 00:56:57,917
We found something.

903
00:56:59,792 --> 00:57:01,750
A chance, maybe.

904
00:57:03,708 --> 00:57:06,292
Don't.

905
00:57:07,292 --> 00:57:08,583
Don't what?

906
00:57:11,625 --> 00:57:13,167
Don't give me hope.

907
00:57:16,667 --> 00:57:18,958
I'm sorry I couldn't give it
to you sooner.

908
00:57:34,125 --> 00:57:38,124
<i>♪ I had a dream last night
I was piloting a plane ♪</i>

909
00:57:38,125 --> 00:57:40,541
<i>♪ And all the passengers
Were drunk and insane ♪</i>

910
00:57:40,542 --> 00:57:41,917
You're drifting left.

911
00:57:42,500 --> 00:57:44,083
One side there, Lebowski.

912
00:57:45,333 --> 00:57:47,332
<i>♪ Shot up a horde of zombies ♪</i>

913
00:57:47,333 --> 00:57:48,624
Ratchet, how's it going?

914
00:57:48,625 --> 00:57:49,916
It's Rocket.

915
00:57:49,917 --> 00:57:52,499
Take it easy. You're only
a genius on Earth, pal.

916
00:57:57,375 --> 00:57:58,958
Time travel suit,
not bad.

917
00:58:00,375 --> 00:58:01,999
Hey, hey, hey! Easy! Easy!

918
00:58:02,000 --> 00:58:03,291
I'm being very careful.

919
00:58:03,292 --> 00:58:04,749
No, you're being very Hulky.

920
00:58:04,750 --> 00:58:05,707
I'm being careful.

921
00:58:05,708 --> 00:58:07,374
These are Pym Particles,
all right?

922
00:58:07,375 --> 00:58:09,624
And ever since Hank Pym
got snapped out of existence,

923
00:58:09,625 --> 00:58:11,332
this is it.
This is what we have.

924
00:58:11,333 --> 00:58:12,416
We're not making any more.

925
00:58:12,417 --> 00:58:13,875
- Scott, calm down.
-  Sorry.

926
00:58:14,417 --> 00:58:16,582
We've got enough
for one round-trip each.

927
00:58:16,583 --> 00:58:18,416
That's it. No do-overs.

928
00:58:18,417 --> 00:58:20,417
Plus, two test runs.

929
00:58:25,042 --> 00:58:27,124
One test run.

930
00:58:27,125 --> 00:58:28,916
All right.
I'm not ready for this.

931
00:58:28,917 --> 00:58:29,917
I'm game.

932
00:58:32,375 --> 00:58:33,417
I'll do it.

933
00:58:34,667 --> 00:58:36,249
Clint, now,
you're gonna feel a little

934
00:58:36,250 --> 00:58:38,416
discombobulated from
the chronoshift. Don't worry.

935
00:58:38,417 --> 00:58:39,791
Wait.
Let me ask you something.

936
00:58:39,792 --> 00:58:42,291
If we can do this,
you know, go back in time,

937
00:58:42,292 --> 00:58:45,083
why don't we just find
baby Thanos, you know, and...

938
00:58:49,458 --> 00:58:50,541
First of all,
that's horrible.

939
00:58:50,542 --> 00:58:51,624
It's Thanos.

940
00:58:51,625 --> 00:58:53,916
And secondly,
time doesn't work that way.

941
00:58:53,917 --> 00:58:56,166
Changing the past
doesn't change the future.

942
00:58:56,167 --> 00:58:57,749
Look, we go back,
we get the stones

943
00:58:57,750 --> 00:58:59,291
before Thanos gets them,

944
00:58:59,292 --> 00:59:00,832
Thanos doesn't have
the stones.

945
00:59:00,833 --> 00:59:01,999
Problem solved.

946
00:59:02,000 --> 00:59:03,791
- Bingo.
- That's not how it works.

947
00:59:03,792 --> 00:59:04,874
Well, that's what I heard.

948
00:59:04,875 --> 00:59:06,166
Wait, but who?
Who told you that?

949
00:59:06,167 --> 00:59:08,249
<i>Star Trek</i>, <i>Terminator</i>,
<i>Timecop</i>.

950
00:59:08,250 --> 00:59:09,999
- <i>Time After Time</i>.
- <i>Quantum Leap</i>.

951
00:59:10,000 --> 00:59:11,541
<i>Wrinkle in Time</i>,
<i>Somewhere in Time</i>.

952
00:59:11,542 --> 00:59:13,291
- <i>Hot Tub Time Machine</i>.
- <i>Hot Tub Time Machine</i>.

953
00:59:13,292 --> 00:59:14,832
<i>Bill and Ted's
Excellent Adventure</i>.

954
00:59:14,833 --> 00:59:17,416
Basically, any movie
that deals with time travel.

955
00:59:17,417 --> 00:59:18,874
<i>Die Hard</i>. No, that's not one.

956
00:59:18,875 --> 00:59:20,207
This is known.

957
00:59:20,208 --> 00:59:21,624
I don't know why
everyone believes that,

958
00:59:21,625 --> 00:59:22,707
but that isn't true.

959
00:59:22,708 --> 00:59:24,666
Think about it.
If you travel to the past,

960
00:59:24,667 --> 00:59:27,332
that past becomes your future.

961
00:59:27,333 --> 00:59:30,541
And your former present
becomes the past,

962
00:59:30,542 --> 00:59:33,207
which can't now be
changed by your new future.

963
00:59:33,208 --> 00:59:34,417
Exactly.

964
00:59:35,042 --> 00:59:37,417
So <i>Back to the Future</i> is
a bunch of bullshit?

965
00:59:41,792 --> 00:59:43,832
All right, Clint.

966
00:59:43,833 --> 00:59:45,292
We're going in three...

967
00:59:46,000 --> 00:59:47,082
two...

968
00:59:47,083 --> 00:59:48,417
one.

969
01:01:00,500 --> 01:01:01,874
Cooper?

970
01:01:01,875 --> 01:01:03,499
Where are my headphones?

971
01:01:03,500 --> 01:01:04,541
Lila?

972
01:01:04,542 --> 01:01:06,791
-  I never had them.
- Lila?

973
01:01:06,792 --> 01:01:09,375
Yeah, you had them yesterday!

974
01:01:10,167 --> 01:01:11,750
Lila! Lila!

975
01:01:17,042 --> 01:01:18,083
Yeah, Dad?

976
01:01:21,833 --> 01:01:22,875
Dad?

977
01:01:25,292 --> 01:01:26,374
Lila!

978
01:01:32,500 --> 01:01:34,999
Hey. Hey, look at me.

979
01:01:35,000 --> 01:01:36,208
You okay?

980
01:01:36,875 --> 01:01:38,916
Yeah. Yeah.

981
01:01:40,625 --> 01:01:41,958
It worked.

982
01:01:43,667 --> 01:01:44,708
It worked.

983
01:01:48,167 --> 01:01:49,875
Okay.
So the how works.

984
01:01:50,583 --> 01:01:53,833
Now, we gotta figure out
the when and the where.

985
01:01:54,833 --> 01:01:56,666
Almost everyone in this room
has had an encounter

986
01:01:56,667 --> 01:01:58,374
with at least one
of the six Infinity Stones.

987
01:01:58,375 --> 01:01:59,916
Or substitute
the word "encounter"

988
01:01:59,917 --> 01:02:01,249
for "damn near been killed"

989
01:02:01,250 --> 01:02:02,874
by one of
the six Infinity Stones.

990
01:02:02,875 --> 01:02:04,082
Well, I haven't.

991
01:02:04,083 --> 01:02:05,166
But I don't even know

992
01:02:05,167 --> 01:02:06,624
what the hell
you're all talking about.

993
01:02:06,625 --> 01:02:09,666
Regardless, we only have
enough Pym Particles

994
01:02:09,667 --> 01:02:11,582
for one round-trip each.

995
01:02:11,583 --> 01:02:13,791
And these stones have been
in a lot of different places

996
01:02:13,792 --> 01:02:14,874
throughout history.

997
01:02:14,875 --> 01:02:16,416
Our history.

998
01:02:16,417 --> 01:02:18,207
So, not a lot of
convenient spots

999
01:02:18,208 --> 01:02:19,499
to just drop in, yeah?

1000
01:02:19,500 --> 01:02:21,832
Which means
we have to pick our targets.

1001
01:02:21,833 --> 01:02:22,916
Correct.

1002
01:02:22,917 --> 01:02:25,832
So, let's start
with the Aether.

1003
01:02:25,833 --> 01:02:27,375
Thor, what do you know?

1004
01:02:33,042 --> 01:02:34,457
Is he asleep?

1005
01:02:34,458 --> 01:02:36,792
No, no.
I'm pretty sure he's dead.

1006
01:02:39,917 --> 01:02:41,333
Uh, where to start? Um...

1007
01:02:43,417 --> 01:02:45,833
The Aether, firstly,
is not a stone.

1008
01:02:46,375 --> 01:02:48,250
Someone called it
a stone before.

1009
01:02:48,917 --> 01:02:53,582
Um, it's more of an angry
sludge sort of a thing, so...

1010
01:02:53,583 --> 01:02:55,457
someone's gonna need
to amend that

1011
01:02:55,458 --> 01:02:56,542
and stop saying that.

1012
01:02:57,083 --> 01:02:59,791
Here's an interesting story,
though, about the Aether.

1013
01:02:59,792 --> 01:03:01,749
My grandfather,
many years ago...

1014
01:03:01,750 --> 01:03:05,666
had to hide the stone
from the Dark Elves.

1015
01:03:05,667 --> 01:03:08,291
Ooh.  Scary beings.

1016
01:03:08,292 --> 01:03:10,000
So, Jane, actually...

1017
01:03:10,792 --> 01:03:12,042
Oh, there she is.

1018
01:03:12,583 --> 01:03:15,792
Yeah, so Jane was
an old flame of mine.

1019
01:03:17,083 --> 01:03:20,374
You know, she stuck her hand
inside a rock this one time,

1020
01:03:20,375 --> 01:03:23,167
and then the Aether
stuck itself inside her,

1021
01:03:23,708 --> 01:03:25,541
and she became
very, very sick.

1022
01:03:25,542 --> 01:03:27,624
And so I had to
take her to Asgard,

1023
01:03:27,625 --> 01:03:28,707
which is where I'm from,

1024
01:03:28,708 --> 01:03:30,957
and we had to try and fix her.

1025
01:03:30,958 --> 01:03:32,749
We were dating at the time,
you see,

1026
01:03:32,750 --> 01:03:35,625
and I got to introduce her
to my mother...

1027
01:03:37,375 --> 01:03:39,583
who's dead, and, um...

1028
01:03:41,042 --> 01:03:44,499
Oh, you know, Jane and I
aren't even dating anymore,

1029
01:03:44,500 --> 01:03:45,416
so...

1030
01:03:45,417 --> 01:03:46,874
Yes, these things happen,
though, you know?

1031
01:03:46,875 --> 01:03:48,374
Nothing lasts forever.
The only thing that...

1032
01:03:48,375 --> 01:03:49,791
- Why don't you come sit down?
- I'm not done yet.

1033
01:03:49,792 --> 01:03:51,791
The only thing that is
permanent in life

1034
01:03:51,792 --> 01:03:53,749
is impermanence.

1035
01:03:53,750 --> 01:03:56,499
Awesome. Eggs? Breakfast?

1036
01:03:56,500 --> 01:03:58,749
No. I'd like a Bloody Mary.

1037
01:03:58,750 --> 01:04:01,707
Quill said he stole
the Power Stone from Morag.

1038
01:04:01,708 --> 01:04:04,667
-  Is that a person?
- No, Morag's a planet.

1039
01:04:05,292 --> 01:04:06,792
Quill was a person.

1040
01:04:07,500 --> 01:04:09,999
Like a planet?
Like in outer space?

1041
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:12,707
Oh, look.
It's like a little puppy,

1042
01:04:12,708 --> 01:04:14,291
all happy and everything.

1043
01:04:14,292 --> 01:04:17,541
Do you wanna go to space?
You wanna go to space, puppy?

1044
01:04:17,542 --> 01:04:18,958
I'll take you to space.

1045
01:04:20,167 --> 01:04:22,166
Thanos found
the Soul Stone on Vormir.

1046
01:04:22,167 --> 01:04:23,667
What is Vormir?

1047
01:04:24,500 --> 01:04:25,583
A dominion of death...

1048
01:04:26,375 --> 01:04:28,708
at the very center
of celestial existence.

1049
01:04:30,083 --> 01:04:34,083
It's where
Thanos murdered my sister.

1050
01:04:40,500 --> 01:04:41,583
Not it.

1051
01:04:43,458 --> 01:04:45,541
-  Time Stone guy.
-  Doctor Strange.

1052
01:04:45,542 --> 01:04:46,999
Yeah,
what kind of doctor was he?

1053
01:04:47,000 --> 01:04:49,082
Ear-nose-throat
meets rabbit-from-hat.

1054
01:04:49,083 --> 01:04:50,707
Nice place
in the Village, though.

1055
01:04:50,708 --> 01:04:51,958
Yeah,
on Sullivan Street?

1056
01:04:52,667 --> 01:04:54,708
-  Bleecker. Was it?
- Wait, he lived in New York?

1057
01:04:55,292 --> 01:04:56,374
No,
he lived in Toronto.

1058
01:04:56,375 --> 01:04:57,457
Yeah,
on Bleecker and Sullivan.

1059
01:04:57,458 --> 01:04:58,582
Have you been listening
to anything?

1060
01:04:58,583 --> 01:04:59,666
Guys.

1061
01:04:59,667 --> 01:05:01,374
If you pick the right year,

1062
01:05:01,375 --> 01:05:03,083
there are
three stones in New York.

1063
01:05:05,500 --> 01:05:07,292
Shut the front door.

1064
01:05:09,917 --> 01:05:12,207
All right.
We have a plan.

1065
01:05:12,208 --> 01:05:16,874
Six stones,
three teams, one shot.

1066
01:05:26,458 --> 01:05:28,375
<i>Five years ago, we lost.</i>

1067
01:05:29,833 --> 01:05:31,000
<i>All of us.</i>

1068
01:05:32,958 --> 01:05:34,292
<i>We lost friends.</i>

1069
01:05:35,125 --> 01:05:36,667
<i>We lost family.</i>

1070
01:05:38,833 --> 01:05:40,458
<i>We lost a part of ourselves.</i>

1071
01:05:41,833 --> 01:05:44,125
<i>Today, we have a chance
to take it all back.</i>

1072
01:05:45,708 --> 01:05:48,125
<i>You know your teams.
You know your missions.</i>

1073
01:05:48,708 --> 01:05:51,208
<i>Get the stones. Get them back.</i>

1074
01:05:52,083 --> 01:05:53,416
One round-trip each.

1075
01:05:53,417 --> 01:05:54,500
No mistakes.

1076
01:05:55,042 --> 01:05:56,208
No do-overs.

1077
01:05:56,875 --> 01:05:58,957
Most of us are going
somewhere we know.

1078
01:05:58,958 --> 01:06:01,375
That doesn't mean we should
know what to expect.

1079
01:06:01,917 --> 01:06:02,917
Be careful.

1080
01:06:03,583 --> 01:06:04,917
Look out for each other.

1081
01:06:06,125 --> 01:06:08,083
This is
the fight of our lives,

1082
01:06:08,958 --> 01:06:10,167
and we're gonna win.

1083
01:06:12,583 --> 01:06:13,708
Whatever it takes.

1084
01:06:17,000 --> 01:06:18,457
Good luck.

1085
01:06:18,458 --> 01:06:19,707
He's pretty good at that.

1086
01:06:19,708 --> 01:06:21,166
- Right?
-  All right.

1087
01:06:21,167 --> 01:06:22,082
You heard the man.

1088
01:06:22,083 --> 01:06:23,500
Stroke those keys,
Jolly Green.

1089
01:06:24,375 --> 01:06:26,000
Trackers engaged.

1090
01:06:26,625 --> 01:06:28,666
You promise to bring that
back in one piece, right?

1091
01:06:28,667 --> 01:06:30,207
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1092
01:06:30,208 --> 01:06:31,708
Okay, I'll do my best.

1093
01:06:32,208 --> 01:06:34,125
As promises go,
that was pretty lame.

1094
01:06:36,250 --> 01:06:38,333
See ya in a minute.

1095
01:07:32,583 --> 01:07:34,166
All right,
we all have our assignments.

1096
01:07:34,167 --> 01:07:36,541
Two stones uptown,
one stone down.

1097
01:07:36,542 --> 01:07:38,541
Stay low.
Keep an eye on the clock.

1098
01:07:54,042 --> 01:07:55,708
Maybe smash a few things
along the way.

1099
01:07:56,917 --> 01:07:59,000
I think it's gratuitous,
but whatever.

1100
01:08:26,542 --> 01:08:28,124
I'd be careful going that way.

1101
01:08:28,125 --> 01:08:29,708
We just had the floors waxed.

1102
01:08:35,000 --> 01:08:36,667
Yeah, I'm looking for
Doctor Strange.

1103
01:08:38,375 --> 01:08:41,083
You're about
five years too early.

1104
01:08:41,833 --> 01:08:44,082
Stephen Strange is
currently performing surgery

1105
01:08:44,083 --> 01:08:45,792
about 20 blocks that way.

1106
01:08:47,208 --> 01:08:48,417
What do you want from him?

1107
01:08:49,500 --> 01:08:51,291
That, actually.

1108
01:08:51,292 --> 01:08:52,292
Ah!

1109
01:08:53,667 --> 01:08:56,333
- I'm afraid not.
- Sorry, but I wasn't asking.

1110
01:08:57,208 --> 01:08:58,291
You don't want to do this.

1111
01:08:58,292 --> 01:09:00,166
You're right, I don't.
But I need that stone,

1112
01:09:00,167 --> 01:09:01,791
and I don't have
time to debate it.

1113
01:09:10,667 --> 01:09:12,250
Let's start over, shall we?

1114
01:09:23,792 --> 01:09:24,957
For you, Lady Jane.

1115
01:09:24,958 --> 01:09:27,957
Um, do you have
anything with pants?

1116
01:09:27,958 --> 01:09:29,249
Pants?

1117
01:09:29,250 --> 01:09:31,332
Never mind.
These will be fine. Thank you.

1118
01:09:31,333 --> 01:09:33,125
- Yes, milady.
-  Oh, that's Jane.

1119
01:09:34,958 --> 01:09:36,042
All right.

1120
01:09:37,375 --> 01:09:38,707
Here's the deal, tubby.

1121
01:09:38,708 --> 01:09:39,874
You're gonna charm her,

1122
01:09:39,875 --> 01:09:41,124
and I'm gonna poke her
with this thing

1123
01:09:41,125 --> 01:09:43,749
and extract the Reality Stone,
and get gone lickety-split.

1124
01:09:45,417 --> 01:09:47,124
I'll be right back, okay?

1125
01:09:47,125 --> 01:09:48,582
The wine cellar
is just down here.

1126
01:09:48,583 --> 01:09:49,666
My father used to have

1127
01:09:49,667 --> 01:09:51,624
this huge barrel
of Aakonian ale.

1128
01:09:51,625 --> 01:09:53,166
I'll see if the scullery has
a couple of to-go cups.

1129
01:09:53,167 --> 01:09:54,957
Hey. Hey! Aren't you
drunk enough already?

1130
01:10:02,292 --> 01:10:03,666
If you could
send Loki some soup.

1131
01:10:03,667 --> 01:10:04,582
Yes, milady.

1132
01:10:04,583 --> 01:10:05,916
And ask our librarians

1133
01:10:05,917 --> 01:10:08,291
to pull some volumes
from the astronomy shelf.

1134
01:10:14,500 --> 01:10:16,167
Who's the fancy broad?

1135
01:10:17,250 --> 01:10:18,667
That's my mother.

1136
01:10:19,375 --> 01:10:20,875
She dies today.

1137
01:10:21,875 --> 01:10:23,875
Oh, that is today?

1138
01:10:30,083 --> 01:10:33,249
I can't do this.
I can't do this.

1139
01:10:33,250 --> 01:10:35,041
I shouldn't be here.
I shouldn't have come.

1140
01:10:35,042 --> 01:10:36,124
This is a bad idea!

1141
01:10:36,125 --> 01:10:38,041
- Come here.
- No, no, no.

1142
01:10:38,042 --> 01:10:40,166
I'm having a panic attack.

1143
01:10:40,167 --> 01:10:41,332
- Come here.
- I shouldn't be here.

1144
01:10:41,333 --> 01:10:42,167
- Right here.
- This is bad.

1145
01:10:42,958 --> 01:10:44,916
You think you're the only one
who lost people?

1146
01:10:44,917 --> 01:10:46,749
What do you think
we're doing here?

1147
01:10:46,750 --> 01:10:48,916
I lost the only family
I ever had.

1148
01:10:48,917 --> 01:10:51,666
Quill, Groot, Drax,
the chick with the antenna,

1149
01:10:51,667 --> 01:10:52,833
all gone.

1150
01:10:53,792 --> 01:10:55,125
I get you miss your mom...

1151
01:10:55,417 --> 01:10:56,791
but she's gone.

1152
01:10:56,792 --> 01:10:57,792
Really gone.

1153
01:10:58,333 --> 01:11:01,291
And there are plenty of people
who are only kinda gone...

1154
01:11:01,292 --> 01:11:02,500
and you can help them.

1155
01:11:03,708 --> 01:11:05,249
So, is it too much to ask

1156
01:11:05,250 --> 01:11:06,999
that you brush
the crumbs outta your beard,

1157
01:11:07,000 --> 01:11:09,749
make schmoopy talk
to Pretty Pants,

1158
01:11:09,750 --> 01:11:12,874
and when she's not looking,
suck out the Infinity Stone

1159
01:11:12,875 --> 01:11:14,375
and help me
get my family back?

1160
01:11:15,333 --> 01:11:17,082
Okay.

1161
01:11:17,083 --> 01:11:18,333
Are you crying?

1162
01:11:19,208 --> 01:11:20,292
No.

1163
01:11:22,125 --> 01:11:23,291
Yes.

1164
01:11:23,292 --> 01:11:24,791
I feel like I'm losing it.

1165
01:11:24,792 --> 01:11:25,832
Get it together!

1166
01:11:25,833 --> 01:11:28,041
You can do this.

1167
01:11:28,042 --> 01:11:29,375
You can do this.

1168
01:11:32,417 --> 01:11:33,417
All right?

1169
01:11:33,917 --> 01:11:34,832
Yes, I can.

1170
01:11:34,833 --> 01:11:35,917
Good.

1171
01:11:38,083 --> 01:11:40,417
I can do this. I can do this.

1172
01:11:41,500 --> 01:11:42,957
I can't do this.

1173
01:11:42,958 --> 01:11:44,916
All right, heartbreaker,
she's alone.

1174
01:11:44,917 --> 01:11:46,499
This is our shot.

1175
01:11:46,500 --> 01:11:49,208
Thor? Thor!

1176
01:11:59,375 --> 01:12:00,750
All right,
bring it down, Blue.

1177
01:12:01,292 --> 01:12:03,208
Right on that line. That's it.
Down, down.

1178
01:12:08,250 --> 01:12:09,791
Hey, can we hurry it up?

1179
01:12:09,792 --> 01:12:11,916
Guys, chop-chop. Come on.
We're on the clock.

1180
01:12:11,917 --> 01:12:13,833
All that is really helpful.

1181
01:12:16,083 --> 01:12:17,333
- Take care, okay?
- Yeah.

1182
01:12:17,875 --> 01:12:20,042
Get that stone and come back.
No messing around.

1183
01:12:20,542 --> 01:12:22,582
- Hey.
- We got this.

1184
01:12:22,583 --> 01:12:23,791
- Let's get it done.
- Yes, sir.

1185
01:12:23,792 --> 01:12:24,875
I'll see you back.

1186
01:12:26,000 --> 01:12:27,874
You guys watch
each other's six.

1187
01:12:27,875 --> 01:12:29,167
Yeah.

1188
01:12:37,792 --> 01:12:39,375
Coordinates
for Vormir are laid in.

1189
01:12:40,958 --> 01:12:42,957
All they have to do
is not fall out.

1190
01:12:49,000 --> 01:12:51,249
We're a long way
from Budapest.

1191
01:12:56,000 --> 01:12:57,542
Okay, so, uh...

1192
01:12:58,833 --> 01:13:02,041
we just wait around
for this Quill guy to show up

1193
01:13:02,042 --> 01:13:04,042
and then he leads us to
the Power Stone, is that it?

1194
01:13:05,125 --> 01:13:06,458
Let's take cover.

1195
01:13:07,583 --> 01:13:09,707
We're not
the only ones in 2014

1196
01:13:09,708 --> 01:13:10,791
looking for the stones.

1197
01:13:10,792 --> 01:13:12,374
Wait a minute. What are you
talking about right now?

1198
01:13:12,375 --> 01:13:13,458
Who else is
looking for these stones?

1199
01:13:17,083 --> 01:13:18,125
My father...

1200
01:13:18,625 --> 01:13:19,708
my sister...

1201
01:13:20,667 --> 01:13:21,916
and me.

1202
01:13:21,917 --> 01:13:23,083
And you?

1203
01:13:24,875 --> 01:13:26,542
Where are you right now?

1204
01:13:55,292 --> 01:13:56,541
You're welcome.

1205
01:13:56,542 --> 01:13:58,792
I didn't ask for your help.

1206
01:13:59,375 --> 01:14:01,874
And yet, you always need it.

1207
01:14:05,167 --> 01:14:07,457
Get up. Father wants us
back on the ship.

1208
01:14:07,458 --> 01:14:08,374
Why?

1209
01:14:08,375 --> 01:14:10,500
He's found an Infinity Stone.

1210
01:14:14,958 --> 01:14:16,582
Where?

1211
01:14:16,583 --> 01:14:18,333
On a planet called Morag.

1212
01:14:19,958 --> 01:14:21,916
Father's plan
is finally in motion.

1213
01:14:21,917 --> 01:14:24,207
One stone isn't six, Nebula.

1214
01:14:24,208 --> 01:14:25,582
It's a start.

1215
01:14:25,583 --> 01:14:27,375
If he gets all of them...

1216
01:14:40,375 --> 01:14:42,207
Ronan's located
the Power Stone.

1217
01:14:42,208 --> 01:14:43,957
I'm dispatching you
to his ship.

1218
01:14:43,958 --> 01:14:45,332
He won't like that.

1219
01:14:45,333 --> 01:14:47,583
His alternative is death.

1220
01:14:49,083 --> 01:14:50,833
Ronan's obsession...

1221
01:14:51,875 --> 01:14:54,042
clouds his judgment.

1222
01:14:58,458 --> 01:15:00,250
We will not fail you, Father.

1223
01:15:01,292 --> 01:15:02,917
No, you won't.

1224
01:15:05,625 --> 01:15:06,625
I swear...

1225
01:15:08,500 --> 01:15:10,417
I will make you proud.

1226
01:15:18,792 --> 01:15:20,499
<i>...we just wait around</i>

1227
01:15:20,500 --> 01:15:22,082
<i>for this Quill guy
to show up...</i>

1228
01:15:22,083 --> 01:15:23,416
<i>and then he leads us
to the Power Stone,</i>

1229
01:15:23,417 --> 01:15:24,417
<i>is that it?</i>

1230
01:15:24,958 --> 01:15:26,375
<i>Let's take cover.</i>

1231
01:15:27,375 --> 01:15:29,249
<i>We're not the only ones
in 2014</i>

1232
01:15:29,250 --> 01:15:30,250
<i>looking for the stones.</i>

1233
01:15:32,667 --> 01:15:34,291
Who was that?

1234
01:15:34,292 --> 01:15:35,457
I don't know.

1235
01:15:35,458 --> 01:15:37,625
My head is splitting.
I don't know.

1236
01:15:39,083 --> 01:15:42,082
Her synaptic drive was
probably damaged in battle.

1237
01:15:42,083 --> 01:15:43,333
Shh.

1238
01:15:52,292 --> 01:15:54,333
Bring her to my ship.

1239
01:16:01,750 --> 01:16:02,832
Better hustle, Cap.

1240
01:16:02,833 --> 01:16:04,874
Things look like they're
just about wrapped up here.

1241
01:16:04,875 --> 01:16:05,791
<i>Got it.</i>

1242
01:16:05,792 --> 01:16:06,833
<i>I'm approaching
the elevator now.</i>

1243
01:16:13,292 --> 01:16:14,875
If it's all the same to you...

1244
01:16:17,167 --> 01:16:18,708
I'll have that drink now.

1245
01:16:19,250 --> 01:16:20,749
All right,
get him on his feet.

1246
01:16:20,750 --> 01:16:24,041
We can all stand around
posing up a storm later.

1247
01:16:24,042 --> 01:16:25,375
By the way,
feel free to clean up.

1248
01:16:25,917 --> 01:16:28,582
Ugh. Mr. Rogers, I almost
forgot that that suit...

1249
01:16:28,583 --> 01:16:30,707
did nothing for your ass.

1250
01:16:30,708 --> 01:16:31,957
<i>No one asked you
to look, Tony.</i>

1251
01:16:31,958 --> 01:16:32,874
It's ridiculous.

1252
01:16:32,875 --> 01:16:33,708
<i>I think you look great, Cap.</i>

1253
01:16:34,250 --> 01:16:36,707
<i>As far as I'm concerned,
that's America's ass.</i>

1254
01:16:36,708 --> 01:16:38,957
Who gets the,
uh, magic wand?

1255
01:16:38,958 --> 01:16:40,041
S.T.R.I.K.E. team's
coming to secure it.

1256
01:16:51,167 --> 01:16:53,082
We can
take that off your hands.

1257
01:16:53,083 --> 01:16:54,083
By all means.

1258
01:16:56,333 --> 01:16:58,124
Careful with that thing.

1259
01:16:58,125 --> 01:16:59,749
Yeah, unless you want
your mind erased.

1260
01:16:59,750 --> 01:17:00,916
And not in a fun way.

1261
01:17:00,917 --> 01:17:02,166
We promise to be careful.

1262
01:17:02,167 --> 01:17:03,207
<i>Who are these guys?</i>

1263
01:17:03,208 --> 01:17:04,791
They are S.H.I.E.L.D.

1264
01:17:04,792 --> 01:17:07,916
Well, actually Hydra,
but we didn't know that yet.

1265
01:17:07,917 --> 01:17:09,291
<i>Seriously? You didn't?</i>

1266
01:17:09,292 --> 01:17:12,041
<i>I mean,
they look like bad guys.</i>

1267
01:17:12,042 --> 01:17:13,499
You're small,
but you're talking loud.

1268
01:17:13,500 --> 01:17:17,749
On my way down to
coordinate search and rescue.

1269
01:17:17,750 --> 01:17:20,374
I mean, honestly, how do you
keep your food down?

1270
01:17:20,375 --> 01:17:21,792
Shut up.

1271
01:17:22,375 --> 01:17:23,707
Oh. All right,
you're up, little buddy.

1272
01:17:23,708 --> 01:17:25,999
There's our stone.

1273
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:27,291
<i>All right.</i>

1274
01:17:27,292 --> 01:17:28,499
<i>Flick me.</i>

1275
01:17:42,625 --> 01:17:43,707
- Move.
- Hey.

1276
01:17:43,708 --> 01:17:45,541
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.
- Hey, hey. Buddy!

1277
01:17:45,542 --> 01:17:47,499
What do you think? Maximum
occupancy has been reached.

1278
01:17:47,500 --> 01:17:48,624
Take the stairs.

1279
01:17:48,625 --> 01:17:50,291
Yeah. Stop, stop.

1280
01:17:53,375 --> 01:17:56,667
"Take the stairs."
Hate the stairs.

1281
01:17:59,875 --> 01:18:02,416
All right, Cap, I got
our scepter in the elevator...

1282
01:18:02,417 --> 01:18:04,208
just passing the 80th floor.

1283
01:18:05,000 --> 01:18:06,000
On it.

1284
01:18:06,833 --> 01:18:07,832
Head to the lobby.

1285
01:18:07,833 --> 01:18:09,332
<i>All right, I'll see you there.</i>

1286
01:18:09,333 --> 01:18:10,832
Evidence secure.

1287
01:18:10,833 --> 01:18:12,250
We're en route to Doctor List.

1288
01:18:12,958 --> 01:18:15,833
No. No hitches at all,
Mr. Secretary.

1289
01:18:21,250 --> 01:18:23,041
Captain. I thought you
were coordinating

1290
01:18:23,042 --> 01:18:24,374
search and rescue.

1291
01:18:24,375 --> 01:18:25,917
Change of plans.

1292
01:18:29,750 --> 01:18:31,167
Hey, Cap.

1293
01:18:32,458 --> 01:18:33,500
Rumlow.

1294
01:18:39,792 --> 01:18:41,791
I just got a call
from the secretary.

1295
01:18:41,792 --> 01:18:43,667
I'm gonna be running point
on the scepter.

1296
01:18:46,167 --> 01:18:48,417
Sir? I don't understand.

1297
01:18:50,875 --> 01:18:52,832
We got word there may be
an attempt to steal it.

1298
01:18:52,833 --> 01:18:54,624
Sorry, Cap.

1299
01:18:54,625 --> 01:18:56,000
We can't give you the scepter.

1300
01:18:56,500 --> 01:18:58,666
I'm gonna have to
call the director.

1301
01:18:58,667 --> 01:19:00,792
That's okay. Trust me.

1302
01:19:04,375 --> 01:19:05,292
Hail Hydra.

1303
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:21,916
So many stairs!

1304
01:19:33,583 --> 01:19:36,374
Thumbelina, do you copy?
I've got eyes on the prize.

1305
01:19:36,375 --> 01:19:37,457
It is go time.

1306
01:19:37,458 --> 01:19:38,625
<i>Bombs away.</i>

1307
01:19:45,875 --> 01:19:48,416
<i>Is-Is that Axe Body Spray?</i>

1308
01:19:48,417 --> 01:19:50,791
Yeah, I had a can in the desk
for emergencies. Relax.

1309
01:19:50,792 --> 01:19:51,957
Can we focus, please?

1310
01:19:51,958 --> 01:19:53,292
<i>I'm going inside you...</i>

1311
01:19:54,000 --> 01:19:55,000
<i>now.</i>

1312
01:20:00,875 --> 01:20:02,416
May I ask you
where you're going?

1313
01:20:02,417 --> 01:20:04,791
Bit of lunch and then Asgard.
I-I'm sorry, you are...?

1314
01:20:04,792 --> 01:20:05,999
Alexander Pierce.

1315
01:20:06,000 --> 01:20:08,707
He's the man above the folks
behind Nick Fury.

1316
01:20:08,708 --> 01:20:09,999
My friends call me
Mr. Secretary.

1317
01:20:10,000 --> 01:20:10,957
I'm gonna have to ask you

1318
01:20:10,958 --> 01:20:12,791
to turn that prisoner
over to me.

1319
01:20:12,792 --> 01:20:14,416
Loki will be answering to
Odin himself.

1320
01:20:14,417 --> 01:20:16,124
No, he's going to
answer to us.

1321
01:20:16,125 --> 01:20:18,582
Odin can have what's left.
And I'm gonna need that case.

1322
01:20:18,583 --> 01:20:19,624
That's been
S.H.I.E.L.D. property

1323
01:20:19,625 --> 01:20:20,624
for over 70 years.

1324
01:20:20,625 --> 01:20:21,916
Hand over the case, Stark.

1325
01:20:21,917 --> 01:20:23,207
All right,
move it, Stuart Little.

1326
01:20:23,208 --> 01:20:24,541
Things are getting dicey
out here. Let's go.

1327
01:20:24,542 --> 01:20:26,250
I'm not gonna argue who's got
the higher authority here...

1328
01:20:26,792 --> 01:20:28,041
<i>You promise me you won't die?</i>

1329
01:20:28,042 --> 01:20:30,916
We're only giving me
a mild cardiac dysrhythmia.

1330
01:20:30,917 --> 01:20:32,791
<i>That doesn't sound mild.</i>

1331
01:20:32,792 --> 01:20:33,874
I need the case.

1332
01:20:33,875 --> 01:20:34,791
I know you got a lot of pull,

1333
01:20:34,792 --> 01:20:35,707
I'm just saying,
jurisdiction...

1334
01:20:35,708 --> 01:20:36,832
Okay, then give me the case.

1335
01:20:36,833 --> 01:20:39,041
-  Well, jurisdiction...
-  Hand it over.

1336
01:20:39,042 --> 01:20:39,999
Do it, Lang!

1337
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:41,332
- Get your hands off me.
- Window's closing.

1338
01:20:41,333 --> 01:20:42,542
Pull my pin.

1339
01:20:43,083 --> 01:20:44,333
<i>Here goes!</i>

1340
01:20:47,167 --> 01:20:48,708
- Stark?
- Stark?

1341
01:20:50,042 --> 01:20:51,291
He's convulsing. Give him air!

1342
01:20:51,292 --> 01:20:53,000
- Medic!
- Medic!

1343
01:20:53,542 --> 01:20:54,792
Give these guys some help.

1344
01:20:55,292 --> 01:20:57,041
Speak to me.

1345
01:20:57,042 --> 01:20:58,542
Stark,
is it your chest machine?

1346
01:21:01,292 --> 01:21:02,625
Breathe, breathe.

1347
01:21:07,875 --> 01:21:09,124
Good job.
Meet me in the alley.

1348
01:21:09,125 --> 01:21:10,208
I'm gonna grab a quick slice.

1349
01:21:15,917 --> 01:21:17,625
No stairs!

1350
01:21:25,833 --> 01:21:27,332
Come on, Stark, stay with us.

1351
01:21:27,333 --> 01:21:28,416
I'm going to
try something. Okay?

1352
01:21:28,417 --> 01:21:29,375
I have no idea
if it's going to work.

1353
01:21:31,375 --> 01:21:32,291
Yes!

1354
01:21:32,292 --> 01:21:33,916
Oh, that worked a treat.

1355
01:21:33,917 --> 01:21:34,999
Dude, that was so crazy.

1356
01:21:35,000 --> 01:21:36,541
I had no idea
if that was gonna work.

1357
01:21:36,542 --> 01:21:38,707
- The case.
- The case is, uh...

1358
01:21:38,708 --> 01:21:40,708
Where's-- Where's the case?
Where's Loki?

1359
01:21:41,708 --> 01:21:42,791
Loki!

1360
01:21:42,792 --> 01:21:44,457
<i>That wasn't
supposed to happen, was it?</i>

1361
01:21:44,458 --> 01:21:45,499
Oh, we blew it.

1362
01:21:45,500 --> 01:21:47,041
Loki?

1363
01:21:49,042 --> 01:21:50,333
Tony, what's going on?

1364
01:21:51,333 --> 01:21:53,000
Tell me you found that cube.

1365
01:21:55,875 --> 01:21:57,292
Oh, you gotta be shitting me.

1366
01:22:01,375 --> 01:22:03,749
I have eyes on Loki.
14th floor.

1367
01:22:03,750 --> 01:22:05,125
I'm not Loki...

1368
01:22:08,708 --> 01:22:10,333
and I don't wanna hurt you.

1369
01:22:19,208 --> 01:22:20,291
I can do this all day.

1370
01:22:20,292 --> 01:22:21,874
Yeah, I know.

1371
01:22:21,875 --> 01:22:22,875
I know.

1372
01:22:55,583 --> 01:22:56,583
Where did you get this?

1373
01:23:07,875 --> 01:23:10,917
Bucky is alive.

1374
01:23:14,458 --> 01:23:15,500
What?

1375
01:23:30,417 --> 01:23:31,958
That is America's ass.

1376
01:23:36,333 --> 01:23:37,416
Please, please.

1377
01:23:37,417 --> 01:23:39,375
I'm sorry,
I can't help you, Bruce.

1378
01:23:40,417 --> 01:23:42,666
If I give up the Time Stone
to help your reality,

1379
01:23:42,667 --> 01:23:43,582
I'm dooming my own.

1380
01:23:43,583 --> 01:23:45,624
With all due respect,
all right...

1381
01:23:45,625 --> 01:23:48,708
I-I'm not sure the science
really supports that.

1382
01:23:54,167 --> 01:23:56,166
The Infinity Stones create

1383
01:23:56,167 --> 01:23:58,791
what you experience
as the flow of time.

1384
01:23:58,792 --> 01:24:00,374
Remove one of the stones...

1385
01:24:00,375 --> 01:24:02,749
and that flow splits.

1386
01:24:02,750 --> 01:24:05,374
Now, this may benefit
your reality...

1387
01:24:05,375 --> 01:24:07,500
but my new one, not so much.

1388
01:24:08,042 --> 01:24:09,624
In this new branch reality...

1389
01:24:09,625 --> 01:24:11,457
without our chief weapon

1390
01:24:11,458 --> 01:24:12,833
against
the forces of darkness...

1391
01:24:13,375 --> 01:24:15,207
our world would be overrun.

1392
01:24:15,208 --> 01:24:17,207
Millions will suffer.

1393
01:24:17,208 --> 01:24:18,458
So, tell me, Doctor.

1394
01:24:19,042 --> 01:24:21,249
Can your science
prevent all that?

1395
01:24:21,250 --> 01:24:22,375
No...

1396
01:24:23,375 --> 01:24:24,541
but we can erase it.

1397
01:24:24,542 --> 01:24:26,541
Because once we're done
with the stones...

1398
01:24:26,542 --> 01:24:28,791
we can return each one
to its own timeline...

1399
01:24:28,792 --> 01:24:30,541
at the moment it was taken.

1400
01:24:30,542 --> 01:24:33,000
So, chronologically...

1401
01:24:34,042 --> 01:24:35,083
in that reality...

1402
01:24:37,667 --> 01:24:39,333
it never left.

1403
01:24:41,708 --> 01:24:44,375
Yes, but you're leaving out
the most important part.

1404
01:24:48,375 --> 01:24:50,874
In order to return the stones,
you have to survive.

1405
01:24:50,875 --> 01:24:53,583
We will. I will. I promise.

1406
01:24:54,417 --> 01:24:56,458
I can't risk this reality
on a promise.

1407
01:24:58,125 --> 01:25:00,791
It's the duty of
the Sorcerer Supreme

1408
01:25:00,792 --> 01:25:02,750
to protect the Time Stone.

1409
01:25:03,292 --> 01:25:05,000
Then why the hell
did Strange give it away?

1410
01:25:06,958 --> 01:25:08,082
What did you say?

1411
01:25:08,083 --> 01:25:10,542
Strange. He gave it away.
He gave it to Thanos.

1412
01:25:11,167 --> 01:25:12,750
- Willingly?
- Yes.

1413
01:25:16,667 --> 01:25:18,416
- Why?
- I have no idea.

1414
01:25:18,417 --> 01:25:20,167
Maybe he made a mistake.

1415
01:25:30,292 --> 01:25:31,583
Or I did.

1416
01:25:51,833 --> 01:25:54,250
Strange is meant to be
the best of us.

1417
01:25:54,792 --> 01:25:56,917
So, he must've done it
for a reason.

1418
01:25:57,708 --> 01:25:59,333
I fear you might be right.

1419
01:26:04,500 --> 01:26:05,500
Thank you.

1420
01:26:11,750 --> 01:26:13,417
I'm counting on you, Bruce.

1421
01:26:15,458 --> 01:26:16,667
We all are.

1422
01:26:37,125 --> 01:26:38,667
Run diagnostics.

1423
01:26:39,417 --> 01:26:41,375
Show me her memory file.

1424
01:26:42,958 --> 01:26:45,417
Sire,
the file appears entangled.

1425
01:26:46,583 --> 01:26:48,542
It was a memory, but not hers.

1426
01:26:49,792 --> 01:26:52,667
There's another consciousness
sharing her network.

1427
01:26:53,208 --> 01:26:54,542
Another Nebula.

1428
01:26:56,667 --> 01:26:58,291
Impossible.

1429
01:26:58,292 --> 01:27:00,917
This duplicate
carries a time stamp...

1430
01:27:01,833 --> 01:27:04,000
from nine years in the future.

1431
01:27:08,583 --> 01:27:11,083
Where is this other Nebula?

1432
01:27:11,750 --> 01:27:13,750
In our solar system on Morag.

1433
01:27:15,292 --> 01:27:16,749
Can you access her?

1434
01:27:16,750 --> 01:27:18,957
Yes, the two are linked.

1435
01:27:18,958 --> 01:27:21,082
Search the duplicate's
memories...

1436
01:27:21,083 --> 01:27:23,417
for Infinity Stones.

1437
01:27:26,958 --> 01:27:29,541
<i>And these stones have been in
a lot of different places</i>

1438
01:27:29,542 --> 01:27:31,249
<i>- throughout history.
- Our history.</i>

1439
01:27:31,250 --> 01:27:33,166
<i>So, not a lot of
convenient spots</i>

1440
01:27:33,167 --> 01:27:34,457
<i>to just drop in.</i>

1441
01:27:34,458 --> 01:27:36,167
<i>Which means we have to
pick our targets.</i>

1442
01:27:36,667 --> 01:27:37,958
- <i>Correct.</i>
- Freeze image.

1443
01:27:39,958 --> 01:27:41,250
Terrans.

1444
01:27:42,208 --> 01:27:43,875
Avengers.

1445
01:27:44,958 --> 01:27:46,832
Unruly wretches.

1446
01:27:46,833 --> 01:27:48,333
What's that reflection?

1447
01:27:49,958 --> 01:27:51,125
Amplify this, Maw.

1448
01:27:54,625 --> 01:27:55,833
I don't understand.

1449
01:28:00,542 --> 01:28:02,291
Two Nebulas.

1450
01:28:02,292 --> 01:28:04,708
No. The same Nebula...

1451
01:28:05,500 --> 01:28:07,250
from two different times.

1452
01:28:08,542 --> 01:28:10,249
Set course for Morag.

1453
01:28:10,250 --> 01:28:12,708
And scan
the duplicate's memories.

1454
01:28:13,458 --> 01:28:15,833
I wanna see everything.

1455
01:28:25,625 --> 01:28:27,541
My ladies, I'll see you after.

1456
01:28:27,542 --> 01:28:29,166
I'll see you after.
Go on ahead.

1457
01:28:43,458 --> 01:28:44,707
What are you doing?

1458
01:28:46,083 --> 01:28:47,457
Oh, God!

1459
01:28:47,458 --> 01:28:50,082
You're better off leaving
the sneaking to your brother.

1460
01:28:50,083 --> 01:28:51,958
No, I wasn't sneaking.
I was just going for a walk.

1461
01:28:52,458 --> 01:28:53,624
What are you wearing?

1462
01:28:53,625 --> 01:28:56,082
Oh, I always wear this.
It's one of my favorites.

1463
01:28:58,875 --> 01:29:00,082
Mmm.

1464
01:29:00,083 --> 01:29:01,624
What's wrong with your eye?

1465
01:29:01,625 --> 01:29:02,707
Oh, my eye.

1466
01:29:02,708 --> 01:29:04,916
Remember
the Battle of Harokin...

1467
01:29:04,917 --> 01:29:08,000
when I got hit in the face
with the broadsword?

1468
01:29:11,542 --> 01:29:13,583
You're not the Thor I know
at all, are you?

1469
01:29:14,333 --> 01:29:16,083
Yes, I am.

1470
01:29:16,583 --> 01:29:19,083
The future hasn't been
kind to you, has it?

1471
01:29:19,542 --> 01:29:21,458
I didn't say I was
from the future.

1472
01:29:21,917 --> 01:29:24,458
I was raised by witches, boy.

1473
01:29:25,500 --> 01:29:27,875
I see with more than eyes,
you know that.

1474
01:29:29,958 --> 01:29:32,374
Yeah,
I'm totally from the future.

1475
01:29:32,375 --> 01:29:34,166
Yes, you are, honey.

1476
01:29:34,167 --> 01:29:35,832
I really need to talk to you.

1477
01:29:35,833 --> 01:29:38,041
We can talk.

1478
01:30:00,958 --> 01:30:02,917
His head was over there...

1479
01:30:03,542 --> 01:30:06,042
and his body over there...

1480
01:30:06,917 --> 01:30:09,833
I mean, what was
the point? I was too late.

1481
01:30:10,500 --> 01:30:12,125
I was just standing there.

1482
01:30:13,083 --> 01:30:14,999
Some idiot with an axe.

1483
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:16,708
Now, you're no idiot.

1484
01:30:17,833 --> 01:30:19,624
You're here, aren't you?

1485
01:30:19,625 --> 01:30:22,083
Seeking counsel from
the wisest person in Asgard.

1486
01:30:22,500 --> 01:30:23,624
I am. Yes.

1487
01:30:23,625 --> 01:30:25,124
Idiot, no.

1488
01:30:25,125 --> 01:30:26,957
A failure?

1489
01:30:26,958 --> 01:30:27,957
Absolutely.

1490
01:30:27,958 --> 01:30:30,041
That's a little bit harsh.

1491
01:30:30,042 --> 01:30:31,542
Do you know what
that makes you?

1492
01:30:32,750 --> 01:30:34,916
Just like everyone else.

1493
01:30:34,917 --> 01:30:37,041
I'm not supposed to be
like everyone else, am I?

1494
01:30:37,042 --> 01:30:41,458
Mmm. Everyone fails at who
they're supposed to be, Thor.

1495
01:30:42,167 --> 01:30:45,374
The measure of a person,
of a hero...

1496
01:30:45,375 --> 01:30:48,750
is how well they succeed
at being who they are.

1497
01:30:54,000 --> 01:30:55,458
I've really missed you, Mom.

1498
01:31:00,458 --> 01:31:03,083
Thor! I got it!

1499
01:31:03,958 --> 01:31:05,500
Get that rabbit!

1500
01:31:08,500 --> 01:31:10,249
Mom, I have to
tell you something.

1501
01:31:10,250 --> 01:31:12,207
No, son, you don't.

1502
01:31:12,208 --> 01:31:14,874
You're here to repair
your future, not mine.

1503
01:31:14,875 --> 01:31:16,624
This is about your future.

1504
01:31:16,625 --> 01:31:18,042
It's none of my business.

1505
01:31:22,042 --> 01:31:23,457
Hi.

1506
01:31:23,458 --> 01:31:25,624
You must be Mom.

1507
01:31:25,625 --> 01:31:27,124
I got the thing.
Come on. We gotta move.

1508
01:31:27,125 --> 01:31:28,874
I wish we had more time.

1509
01:31:28,875 --> 01:31:30,874
No, this was a gift.

1510
01:31:30,875 --> 01:31:34,292
Now you go and be the man
you're meant to be.

1511
01:31:34,750 --> 01:31:35,999
I love you, Mom.

1512
01:31:36,000 --> 01:31:36,917
I love you.

1513
01:31:41,375 --> 01:31:43,292
And eat a salad.

1514
01:31:44,292 --> 01:31:45,582
Come on, we gotta go.

1515
01:31:45,583 --> 01:31:47,332
- Goodbye.
-  Three...

1516
01:31:47,333 --> 01:31:48,417
- Two...
- No, wait!

1517
01:31:51,667 --> 01:31:52,916
What am I looking at?

1518
01:31:52,917 --> 01:31:54,500
Oh, sometimes
it takes a second.

1519
01:32:04,375 --> 01:32:06,000
I'm still worthy.

1520
01:32:07,417 --> 01:32:09,042
Oh, boy.

1521
01:32:10,208 --> 01:32:12,125
- Goodbye, Mom.
- Goodbye.

1522
01:32:51,333 --> 01:32:52,958
So, he's an idiot?

1523
01:32:54,292 --> 01:32:55,708
Yeah.

1524
01:33:04,208 --> 01:33:05,582
What's that?

1525
01:33:05,583 --> 01:33:07,458
The tool of a thief.

1526
01:33:15,083 --> 01:33:16,500
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

1527
01:33:17,208 --> 01:33:18,999
This is the part
where spikes come out...

1528
01:33:19,000 --> 01:33:20,582
with skeletons on the end
of them and everything.

1529
01:33:20,583 --> 01:33:21,874
What are you talking about?

1530
01:33:21,875 --> 01:33:22,999
When you break into
a place called

1531
01:33:23,000 --> 01:33:24,457
"The Temple of
the Power Stone"...

1532
01:33:24,458 --> 01:33:25,832
there's gonna be
a bunch of booby traps.

1533
01:33:25,833 --> 01:33:28,167
- Oh, my God.
- Okay. All right. Go ahead.

1534
01:34:01,417 --> 01:34:02,917
I wasn't always like this.

1535
01:34:03,792 --> 01:34:04,874
Me either.

1536
01:34:06,625 --> 01:34:08,083
But we work with
what we got, right?

1537
01:34:10,000 --> 01:34:11,499
Mmm.

1538
01:34:11,500 --> 01:34:13,500
Let's sync up.

1539
01:34:15,375 --> 01:34:17,833
Three, two, one.

1540
01:34:30,667 --> 01:34:32,457
<i>You murdered
trillions!</i>

1541
01:34:32,458 --> 01:34:34,417
<i>You should be
grateful.</i>

1542
01:34:35,500 --> 01:34:37,249
<i>Where are
the stones?</i>

1543
01:34:37,250 --> 01:34:38,250
<i>Gone.</i>

1544
01:34:39,000 --> 01:34:40,000
<i>Reduced to atoms.</i>

1545
01:34:40,708 --> 01:34:42,375
<i>You used them
two days ago!</i>

1546
01:34:42,750 --> 01:34:45,832
<i>I used the stones
to destroy the stones.</i>

1547
01:34:45,833 --> 01:34:48,124
<i>It nearly killed me.</i>

1548
01:34:48,125 --> 01:34:49,916
<i>But the work is done.</i>

1549
01:34:49,917 --> 01:34:51,750
<i>It always will be.</i>

1550
01:34:53,042 --> 01:34:56,500
<i>I am inevitable.</i>

1551
01:34:57,750 --> 01:34:59,957
What did you do to them?

1552
01:34:59,958 --> 01:35:01,208
Nothing.

1553
01:35:02,083 --> 01:35:03,375
Yet.

1554
01:35:05,167 --> 01:35:06,999
They're not trying to stop
something

1555
01:35:07,000 --> 01:35:08,875
I'm going to do in our time.

1556
01:35:09,292 --> 01:35:11,124
They're trying to undo
something

1557
01:35:11,125 --> 01:35:12,999
I've already done in theirs.

1558
01:35:13,000 --> 01:35:14,667
The stones.

1559
01:35:15,583 --> 01:35:17,500
I found them all.

1560
01:35:19,292 --> 01:35:20,667
I won.

1561
01:35:21,417 --> 01:35:24,375
Tipped the cosmic scales
to balance.

1562
01:35:28,375 --> 01:35:30,125
This is your future.

1563
01:35:30,542 --> 01:35:32,500
It's my destiny.

1564
01:35:33,708 --> 01:35:35,916
<i>My father is
many things.</i>

1565
01:35:35,917 --> 01:35:37,750
<i>A liar is not one of them.</i>

1566
01:35:39,292 --> 01:35:40,458
<i>Ah.</i>

1567
01:35:41,458 --> 01:35:43,541
<i>Thank you, daughter.</i>

1568
01:35:43,542 --> 01:35:45,791
<i>Perhaps I treated you
too harshly.</i>

1569
01:35:50,208 --> 01:35:53,083
And that is destiny fulfilled.

1570
01:35:53,500 --> 01:35:55,041
Sire...

1571
01:35:55,042 --> 01:35:56,207
your daughter...

1572
01:35:58,625 --> 01:35:59,625
No!

1573
01:36:00,083 --> 01:36:01,291
...is a traitor.

1574
01:36:01,292 --> 01:36:03,916
That's not me.
It's not, I could never...

1575
01:36:03,917 --> 01:36:05,249
I would never betray you.

1576
01:36:05,250 --> 01:36:07,083
Never. Never.

1577
01:36:12,833 --> 01:36:14,000
I know.

1578
01:36:14,958 --> 01:36:18,208
And you'll have the chance
to prove it.

1579
01:36:24,500 --> 01:36:25,583
No!

1580
01:36:26,292 --> 01:36:28,541
He knows!

1581
01:36:32,083 --> 01:36:34,749
Barton! Barton, come in.

1582
01:36:34,750 --> 01:36:36,042
Romanoff!

1583
01:36:36,667 --> 01:36:38,249
Come in, we have a problem.

1584
01:36:38,250 --> 01:36:39,541
Come on!

1585
01:36:39,542 --> 01:36:41,124
Come in, we have a...

1586
01:36:41,125 --> 01:36:42,458
Thanos knows.

1587
01:36:43,125 --> 01:36:44,375
Thanos...

1588
01:36:58,208 --> 01:36:59,292
Cap.

1589
01:37:00,792 --> 01:37:03,124
Sorry, buddy,
we got a problem.

1590
01:37:03,125 --> 01:37:05,208
Yeah, we do.

1591
01:37:05,792 --> 01:37:06,957
Well, what are
we gonna do now?

1592
01:37:06,958 --> 01:37:08,124
You know what?
Give me a break, Steve.

1593
01:37:08,125 --> 01:37:09,707
I just got hit in the head
with the Hulk.

1594
01:37:09,708 --> 01:37:11,291
You said that we had one shot.

1595
01:37:11,292 --> 01:37:12,791
This was our shot.

1596
01:37:12,792 --> 01:37:14,957
We shot it. It's shot.
Six stones or nothing.

1597
01:37:14,958 --> 01:37:16,499
- It was six stones or nothing.
- You're repeating yourself.

1598
01:37:16,500 --> 01:37:17,541
You're repeating yourself.

1599
01:37:17,542 --> 01:37:19,541
- You're repeating yourself.
- Dude. Come on!

1600
01:37:19,542 --> 01:37:21,499
No. You never wanted
a time heist.

1601
01:37:21,500 --> 01:37:22,666
You weren't on board with
the time heist.

1602
01:37:22,667 --> 01:37:23,957
- I dropped the ball.
- You ruined the time heist.

1603
01:37:23,958 --> 01:37:25,416
-  Is that what I did?
-  Yeah.

1604
01:37:25,417 --> 01:37:27,374
Are there any other options
with the Tesseract?

1605
01:37:27,375 --> 01:37:28,624
No, no, no,
there's no other options.

1606
01:37:28,625 --> 01:37:30,166
There's no do-overs.

1607
01:37:30,167 --> 01:37:32,374
We're not going anywhere else.
We have one particle left.

1608
01:37:32,375 --> 01:37:33,291
Each.

1609
01:37:33,292 --> 01:37:35,874
That's it. All right?
We use that...

1610
01:37:35,875 --> 01:37:37,207
bye-bye,
you're not going home.

1611
01:37:37,208 --> 01:37:39,332
Yeah, well, if we don't try...

1612
01:37:39,333 --> 01:37:40,666
then no one else
is going home, either.

1613
01:37:40,667 --> 01:37:41,583
I got it.

1614
01:37:42,875 --> 01:37:44,999
There's another way to retake
the Tesseract

1615
01:37:45,000 --> 01:37:46,917
and acquire new particles.

1616
01:37:47,750 --> 01:37:48,792
Little stroll down
memory lane.

1617
01:37:49,583 --> 01:37:51,417
Military installation,
Garden State.

1618
01:37:55,500 --> 01:37:56,957
When were they both there?

1619
01:37:56,958 --> 01:37:59,999
They were there at a time...
I have a vaguely exact idea.

1620
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:01,041
How vague?

1621
01:38:01,042 --> 01:38:02,207
What are you talking about?
Where are we going?

1622
01:38:02,208 --> 01:38:03,166
I know for a fact
they were there.

1623
01:38:03,167 --> 01:38:05,000
- Who's they? What're we doing?
- And I know how I know.

1624
01:38:07,375 --> 01:38:08,917
Guys, what is it?

1625
01:38:09,500 --> 01:38:11,291
Looks like we're improvising.

1626
01:38:11,292 --> 01:38:12,582
- Great.
- What are we improvising?

1627
01:38:12,583 --> 01:38:14,499
Scott, get this
back to the compound.

1628
01:38:14,500 --> 01:38:15,417
Suit up.

1629
01:38:15,833 --> 01:38:17,374
- What's in New Jersey?
- 0-4.

1630
01:38:17,375 --> 01:38:18,374
0-4.

1631
01:38:18,375 --> 01:38:19,541
- 0-7.
- 0-7.

1632
01:38:19,542 --> 01:38:21,417
- Excuse me.
- 1-9-7-0.

1633
01:38:21,875 --> 01:38:22,957
Are you sure?

1634
01:38:22,958 --> 01:38:24,416
Cap? Captain?

1635
01:38:24,417 --> 01:38:26,416
Steve? Sorry.

1636
01:38:26,417 --> 01:38:28,207
America. Rogers.

1637
01:38:28,208 --> 01:38:29,417
Look, if you do this...

1638
01:38:29,792 --> 01:38:32,250
and it doesn't work,
you're not coming back.

1639
01:38:33,333 --> 01:38:35,125
Thanks for the pep talk, pissant.

1640
01:38:36,167 --> 01:38:37,375
You trust me?

1641
01:38:38,250 --> 01:38:39,417
I do.

1642
01:38:40,458 --> 01:38:41,792
Your call.

1643
01:38:42,667 --> 01:38:44,375
Here we go.

1644
01:39:00,417 --> 01:39:04,167
Hey, man! Make love, not war.

1645
01:39:09,958 --> 01:39:12,791
Clearly you weren't actually
born here, right?

1646
01:39:12,792 --> 01:39:14,292
The idea of me was.

1647
01:39:15,458 --> 01:39:17,166
Right. Well, imagine
you're S.H.I.E.L.D...

1648
01:39:17,167 --> 01:39:20,417
running a quasi-fascistic
intelligence organization...

1649
01:39:21,750 --> 01:39:23,499
where do you hide it?

1650
01:39:23,500 --> 01:39:24,875
In plain sight.

1651
01:39:53,542 --> 01:39:54,832
Good luck on your mission,
Captain.

1652
01:39:54,833 --> 01:39:57,375
Good luck on your project,
Doctor.

1653
01:40:00,792 --> 01:40:01,875
You new here?

1654
01:40:04,333 --> 01:40:05,750
Not exactly.

1655
01:40:12,417 --> 01:40:14,333
Come on, you bastard.

1656
01:40:21,000 --> 01:40:22,500
Gotcha.

1657
01:40:40,042 --> 01:40:41,708
Back in the game.

1658
01:40:44,375 --> 01:40:45,583
Arnim, you in there?

1659
01:40:46,542 --> 01:40:47,583
Arnim?

1660
01:40:52,875 --> 01:40:54,208
Hey!

1661
01:40:54,875 --> 01:40:56,583
The door is this way, pal.

1662
01:40:57,583 --> 01:40:58,458
Oh, yeah.

1663
01:40:59,000 --> 01:41:00,666
Looking for Doctor Zola,
have you seen him?

1664
01:41:00,667 --> 01:41:01,999
Yeah, no, Doctor Zola.

1665
01:41:02,000 --> 01:41:04,166
No, I haven't, haven't,
haven't seen a soul.

1666
01:41:04,167 --> 01:41:05,167
Huh.

1667
01:41:05,667 --> 01:41:06,917
Pardon me.

1668
01:41:07,875 --> 01:41:09,292
Do I know you?

1669
01:41:10,542 --> 01:41:12,125
No, sir. I'm, uh...

1670
01:41:13,000 --> 01:41:14,791
I'm a visitor from MIT.

1671
01:41:14,792 --> 01:41:16,957
Huh. MIT.

1672
01:41:16,958 --> 01:41:18,541
Got a name?

1673
01:41:18,542 --> 01:41:19,832
Howard.

1674
01:41:19,833 --> 01:41:21,416
Well, that'll be easy
to remember.

1675
01:41:21,417 --> 01:41:22,458
Howard...

1676
01:41:23,333 --> 01:41:24,333
Potts.

1677
01:41:24,917 --> 01:41:26,750
Well, I'm, uh, Howard Stark.

1678
01:41:27,292 --> 01:41:28,374
Hi.

1679
01:41:28,375 --> 01:41:29,832
Shake that, don't pull it.

1680
01:41:29,833 --> 01:41:30,833
Yeah.

1681
01:41:32,250 --> 01:41:34,624
You look a little green
around the gills there, Potts.

1682
01:41:34,625 --> 01:41:36,749
Oh, I'm fine. Just long hours.

1683
01:41:36,750 --> 01:41:38,667
Uh... You wanna get some air?

1684
01:41:41,208 --> 01:41:43,166
- Hello, Potts.
- Yeah.

1685
01:41:43,167 --> 01:41:44,582
- That'd be swell.
- That way.

1686
01:41:44,583 --> 01:41:45,707
Okay.

1687
01:41:45,708 --> 01:41:47,375
Need your briefcase?

1688
01:41:51,708 --> 01:41:54,332
You're not one of those
beatniks, are you, Potts?

1689
01:42:00,125 --> 01:42:02,082
- Hello?
-  <i>Doctor Pym?</i>

1690
01:42:02,083 --> 01:42:04,457
That would be the number
that you called, yes.

1691
01:42:04,458 --> 01:42:06,874
<i>This is
Captain Stevens from shipping.</i>

1692
01:42:06,875 --> 01:42:08,291
<i>We have a package for you.</i>

1693
01:42:08,292 --> 01:42:09,707
Oh. Bring it up.

1694
01:42:09,708 --> 01:42:11,667
<i>Well, that's
the thing, sir, we can't.</i>

1695
01:42:12,792 --> 01:42:15,582
I'm confused.
I thought that was your job.

1696
01:42:15,583 --> 01:42:17,124
<i>Well, it's just...</i>

1697
01:42:17,125 --> 01:42:18,749
<i>Sir, the box is glowing,</i>

1698
01:42:18,750 --> 01:42:19,832
<i>and to be honest,</i>

1699
01:42:19,833 --> 01:42:21,707
<i>some of our mail guys
aren't feeling that great.</i>

1700
01:42:21,708 --> 01:42:23,332
They didn't open it, did they?

1701
01:42:23,333 --> 01:42:25,750
<i>Uh, yeah, they did.
You better get down here.</i>

1702
01:42:26,583 --> 01:42:28,500
Excuse me! Out of the way!

1703
01:42:55,667 --> 01:42:58,750
So, flowers and sauerkraut.
You got a big date tonight?

1704
01:42:59,917 --> 01:43:01,541
Uh, my wife's expecting.

1705
01:43:01,542 --> 01:43:04,375
And, uh, too much time
at the office.

1706
01:43:06,208 --> 01:43:07,749
Congratulations.

1707
01:43:07,750 --> 01:43:09,875
- Thanks. Hold this, will ya?
- Yeah, sure.

1708
01:43:10,958 --> 01:43:13,250
- How far along is she?
- Uh, I don't know. Uh...

1709
01:43:14,833 --> 01:43:15,916
She's at the point where

1710
01:43:15,917 --> 01:43:17,583
she can't stand the sound
of my chewing.

1711
01:43:18,125 --> 01:43:21,417
I guess I'll be eating dinner
in the pantry again. Some day.

1712
01:43:22,125 --> 01:43:23,291
I have a little girl.

1713
01:43:23,292 --> 01:43:24,957
A girl would be nice.

1714
01:43:24,958 --> 01:43:26,958
Less of a chance she'd
turn out exactly like me.

1715
01:43:27,625 --> 01:43:29,249
What'd be so awful about that?

1716
01:43:29,250 --> 01:43:31,041
Let's just say that
the, uh, greater good

1717
01:43:31,042 --> 01:43:34,625
has rarely outweighed
my own self-interest.

1718
01:43:38,667 --> 01:43:39,874
And you've never seen
these two men before?

1719
01:43:39,875 --> 01:43:41,874
No, I've got an eye for this.
The two of them looked fishy.

1720
01:43:41,875 --> 01:43:43,041
Can you describe them?

1721
01:43:43,042 --> 01:43:44,291
Well, one of them had
a hippie beard.

1722
01:43:44,292 --> 01:43:46,624
Hippie. Like Bee Gees
or Mungo Jerry?

1723
01:43:46,625 --> 01:43:47,874
Definitely Mungo Jerry.

1724
01:43:47,875 --> 01:43:48,874
Yeah, this is Chesler.

1725
01:43:48,875 --> 01:43:50,166
I need every available MP
to sublevel six.

1726
01:43:50,167 --> 01:43:52,042
We have a potential breach.

1727
01:44:09,917 --> 01:44:11,624
-  I said bring them in.
- They're trying, ma'am,

1728
01:44:11,625 --> 01:44:13,291
but Braddock's unit has been
stopped by lightning strikes.

1729
01:44:13,292 --> 01:44:14,249
Oh, for the love of...

1730
01:44:14,250 --> 01:44:15,957
Well, I'll look at the
weather projections.

1731
01:44:15,958 --> 01:44:18,041
You call Braddock and tell him
to shelter in place.

1732
01:44:18,042 --> 01:44:19,583
Assuming he's bright enough
to come out of the rain.

1733
01:44:31,750 --> 01:44:34,542
Crikey O'Reilly. Sergeant?

1734
01:44:39,875 --> 01:44:41,875
It's not lightning strikes
we're looking at.

1735
01:44:53,458 --> 01:44:55,124
And so,
where you at with names?

1736
01:44:55,125 --> 01:44:58,207
Well, if it's
a boy, my wife likes Elmonzo.

1737
01:44:58,208 --> 01:45:00,499
Huh. Well, you might wanna
let that stew awhile.

1738
01:45:00,500 --> 01:45:01,792
- You got time.
- Uh-huh.

1739
01:45:03,250 --> 01:45:04,750
Let me ask you a question.

1740
01:45:05,750 --> 01:45:09,166
When your kid was born,
were you nervous?

1741
01:45:09,167 --> 01:45:10,749
Wildly.

1742
01:45:10,750 --> 01:45:12,624
- Yeah.
- Did you feel qualified?

1743
01:45:12,625 --> 01:45:14,457
Like you had any idea

1744
01:45:14,458 --> 01:45:16,208
how to successfully
operate that thing?

1745
01:45:16,750 --> 01:45:19,624
I literally pieced it together
as I went along.

1746
01:45:19,625 --> 01:45:21,666
I thought about what
my dad did and...

1747
01:45:21,667 --> 01:45:23,416
My old man,

1748
01:45:23,417 --> 01:45:25,291
he never met a problem
he couldn't solve with a belt.

1749
01:45:25,292 --> 01:45:27,499
I thought my dad was
tough on me.

1750
01:45:27,500 --> 01:45:28,791
And now, looking back on it,

1751
01:45:28,792 --> 01:45:30,374
I just remember
the good stuff.

1752
01:45:30,375 --> 01:45:31,999
You know?
He did drop the odd pearl.

1753
01:45:32,000 --> 01:45:33,500
Yeah? Like what?

1754
01:45:34,625 --> 01:45:37,125
"No amount of money
ever bought a second of time."

1755
01:45:38,458 --> 01:45:39,500
Smart guy.

1756
01:45:39,917 --> 01:45:41,375
He did his best.

1757
01:45:42,750 --> 01:45:44,292
I'll tell you,
that kid's not even here yet,

1758
01:45:44,833 --> 01:45:46,708
and there's nothing
I wouldn't do for him.

1759
01:45:55,458 --> 01:45:56,833
Good to meet you, Potts.

1760
01:45:57,500 --> 01:45:58,333
Yeah.

1761
01:45:58,750 --> 01:45:59,917
Howard...

1762
01:46:00,500 --> 01:46:02,083
everything's gonna be
all right.

1763
01:46:05,083 --> 01:46:06,333
Thank you...

1764
01:46:07,292 --> 01:46:08,625
for everything...

1765
01:46:09,042 --> 01:46:11,333
you've done for this country.

1766
01:46:14,208 --> 01:46:15,333
Jarvis.

1767
01:46:19,042 --> 01:46:20,583
Have we ever met that guy?

1768
01:46:22,583 --> 01:46:24,083
You meet a lot of people, sir.

1769
01:46:26,708 --> 01:46:28,333
Seems very familiar.

1770
01:46:29,250 --> 01:46:30,708
Weird beard.

1771
01:46:39,042 --> 01:46:40,042
You're weak.

1772
01:46:40,583 --> 01:46:41,667
I'm you.

1773
01:46:59,208 --> 01:47:00,625
You could stop this.

1774
01:47:01,667 --> 01:47:03,458
You know you want to.

1775
01:47:04,167 --> 01:47:06,333
Did you see what happens
in the future?

1776
01:47:07,625 --> 01:47:10,000
Thanos finds the Soul Stone.

1777
01:47:11,542 --> 01:47:13,542
You wanna know how
he does that?

1778
01:47:14,917 --> 01:47:19,083
You wanna know what
he does to you?

1779
01:47:19,583 --> 01:47:20,624
That's enough.

1780
01:47:33,250 --> 01:47:34,833
You disgust me.

1781
01:47:36,125 --> 01:47:40,458
But that doesn't mean
you're useless.

1782
01:48:02,792 --> 01:48:04,375
How do I look?

1783
01:48:10,958 --> 01:48:11,958
Wow.

1784
01:48:12,958 --> 01:48:15,042
Under different circumstances,

1785
01:48:16,250 --> 01:48:18,250
this would be totally awesome.

1786
01:48:30,083 --> 01:48:31,249
I bet the raccoon

1787
01:48:31,250 --> 01:48:32,875
didn't have to climb
a mountain.

1788
01:48:33,375 --> 01:48:35,457
Technically he's not
a raccoon, you know?

1789
01:48:35,458 --> 01:48:37,166
Oh, whatever. He eats garbage.

1790
01:48:37,167 --> 01:48:38,500
Welcome.

1791
01:48:41,667 --> 01:48:43,166
Natasha.

1792
01:48:43,167 --> 01:48:44,167
Daughter of Ivan.

1793
01:48:45,500 --> 01:48:46,791
Clint.

1794
01:48:46,792 --> 01:48:49,083
Son of Edith.

1795
01:48:54,458 --> 01:48:55,917
Who are you?

1796
01:48:56,542 --> 01:48:59,166
Consider me a guide...

1797
01:48:59,167 --> 01:49:00,999
to you...

1798
01:49:01,000 --> 01:49:02,999
and to all who seek
the Soul Stone.

1799
01:49:03,000 --> 01:49:04,207
Oh, good.

1800
01:49:04,208 --> 01:49:06,333
You tell us where it is,
then we'll be on our way.

1801
01:49:06,875 --> 01:49:08,792
Oh, <i>liebchen.</i>

1802
01:49:10,250 --> 01:49:12,500
If only it were that easy.

1803
01:49:24,583 --> 01:49:28,292
What you seek
lies in front of you.

1804
01:49:29,542 --> 01:49:31,958
As does what you fear.

1805
01:49:36,875 --> 01:49:38,750
The stone's down there.

1806
01:49:39,375 --> 01:49:40,958
For one of you.

1807
01:49:41,583 --> 01:49:43,292
For the other...

1808
01:49:45,958 --> 01:49:48,041
In order to take the stone,

1809
01:49:48,042 --> 01:49:51,042
you must lose that
which you love.

1810
01:49:52,417 --> 01:49:55,333
An everlasting exchange.

1811
01:49:56,583 --> 01:50:00,667
A soul for a soul.

1812
01:50:03,250 --> 01:50:06,292
How's it going?

1813
01:50:08,042 --> 01:50:09,250
Jesus.

1814
01:50:09,917 --> 01:50:11,500
Maybe he's making
this shit up.

1815
01:50:12,375 --> 01:50:13,708
No.

1816
01:50:14,542 --> 01:50:15,542
I don't think so.

1817
01:50:16,250 --> 01:50:18,417
Why? 'Cause he knows
your daddy's name?

1818
01:50:20,042 --> 01:50:20,958
I didn't.

1819
01:50:22,458 --> 01:50:24,542
Thanos left here
with the stone

1820
01:50:25,500 --> 01:50:27,042
without his daughter.

1821
01:50:27,583 --> 01:50:29,292
That's not a coincidence.

1822
01:50:30,375 --> 01:50:32,000
Yeah.

1823
01:50:33,708 --> 01:50:35,583
Whatever it takes.

1824
01:50:40,083 --> 01:50:41,583
Whatever it takes.

1825
01:50:45,958 --> 01:50:48,082
If we don't get that stone,

1826
01:50:48,083 --> 01:50:49,750
billions of people stay dead.

1827
01:50:50,625 --> 01:50:51,792
Yeah.

1828
01:50:53,667 --> 01:50:55,792
Then I guess we both know
who it's gotta be.

1829
01:50:56,542 --> 01:50:57,708
I guess we do.

1830
01:51:06,125 --> 01:51:07,791
I'm starting to think

1831
01:51:07,792 --> 01:51:10,833
we mean different people
here, Natasha.

1832
01:51:11,333 --> 01:51:13,332
For the last five years, I've
been trying to do one thing.

1833
01:51:13,333 --> 01:51:14,749
Get to right here.

1834
01:51:14,750 --> 01:51:16,916
That's all it's been about.
Bringing everybody back.

1835
01:51:16,917 --> 01:51:19,291
No, don't you get all
decent on me now.

1836
01:51:19,292 --> 01:51:21,292
What, you think I wanna do it?

1837
01:51:21,875 --> 01:51:23,791
I'm trying to save your life,
you idiot.

1838
01:51:23,792 --> 01:51:25,124
Yeah, well,
I don't want you to.

1839
01:51:25,125 --> 01:51:26,125
How's that?

1840
01:51:27,042 --> 01:51:29,250
Natasha, you know
what I've done.

1841
01:51:30,917 --> 01:51:32,708
You know what I've become.

1842
01:51:34,833 --> 01:51:37,417
I don't judge people
on their worst mistakes.

1843
01:51:41,583 --> 01:51:42,833
Maybe you should.

1844
01:51:43,708 --> 01:51:45,250
You didn't.

1845
01:51:51,417 --> 01:51:53,625
You're a pain in my ass,
you know that?

1846
01:52:04,708 --> 01:52:05,957
Okay.

1847
01:52:07,667 --> 01:52:09,167
You win.

1848
01:52:15,625 --> 01:52:16,792
Tell my family I love 'em.

1849
01:52:20,500 --> 01:52:21,749
You tell 'em yourself.

1850
01:52:54,542 --> 01:52:55,542
Damn you.

1851
01:53:03,042 --> 01:53:04,917
Wait.

1852
01:53:12,083 --> 01:53:13,917
Let me go.

1853
01:53:15,167 --> 01:53:16,167
No.

1854
01:53:17,917 --> 01:53:18,917
No. Please, no.

1855
01:53:22,292 --> 01:53:24,125
It's okay.

1856
01:53:26,333 --> 01:53:27,167
Please.

1857
01:53:29,250 --> 01:53:30,250
No!

1858
01:55:11,625 --> 01:55:12,625
Did we get 'em all?

1859
01:55:14,042 --> 01:55:15,833
Are you telling me
this actually worked?

1860
01:55:20,667 --> 01:55:21,875
Clint, where's Nat?

1861
01:55:51,083 --> 01:55:52,083
Do we know if she had family?

1862
01:55:53,250 --> 01:55:54,541
Yeah.

1863
01:55:54,542 --> 01:55:55,624
Us.

1864
01:55:57,000 --> 01:55:58,042
What?

1865
01:55:58,917 --> 01:55:59,999
Huh?

1866
01:56:00,000 --> 01:56:01,332
- What are you doing?
- Just asked him a question.

1867
01:56:01,333 --> 01:56:02,749
Yeah, no, you're
acting like she's dead.

1868
01:56:02,750 --> 01:56:03,874
Why are we acting
like she's dead?

1869
01:56:03,875 --> 01:56:05,374
We have the stones, right?

1870
01:56:05,375 --> 01:56:06,541
As long as we have the stones,

1871
01:56:06,542 --> 01:56:08,457
Cap, we can bring her back.
Isn't that right?

1872
01:56:08,458 --> 01:56:10,624
So, stop this shit. We're
the Avengers. Get it together.

1873
01:56:10,625 --> 01:56:11,833
Can't get her back.

1874
01:56:14,833 --> 01:56:16,249
What's he...? What?

1875
01:56:16,250 --> 01:56:17,458
It can't be undone.

1876
01:56:18,042 --> 01:56:19,750
It can't.

1877
01:56:22,250 --> 01:56:23,582
Look,
I'm sorry, no offense,

1878
01:56:23,583 --> 01:56:25,541
but you're a very
earthly being, okay?

1879
01:56:25,542 --> 01:56:26,874
And we're talking
about space magic.

1880
01:56:26,875 --> 01:56:29,166
And "can't" seems very
definitive. Don't you think?

1881
01:56:29,167 --> 01:56:32,041
Yeah, look, I know that I'm
way outside my pay grade here.

1882
01:56:32,042 --> 01:56:33,791
But she still
isn't here, is she?

1883
01:56:33,792 --> 01:56:34,832
No, that's my point.

1884
01:56:34,833 --> 01:56:38,082
It can't be undone.

1885
01:56:38,083 --> 01:56:41,582
Or that's at least what the
red, floating guy had to say.

1886
01:56:41,583 --> 01:56:43,207
Maybe you wanna
go talk to him, okay?

1887
01:56:43,208 --> 01:56:46,250
Go grab your hammer and you go
fly and you talk to him.

1888
01:56:54,792 --> 01:56:56,833
It was supposed to be me.

1889
01:56:59,083 --> 01:57:01,541
She sacrificed her life
for that goddamn stone.

1890
01:57:01,542 --> 01:57:03,041
She bet her life on it.

1891
01:57:07,917 --> 01:57:10,250
She's not coming back.

1892
01:57:12,042 --> 01:57:13,542
We have to make it worth it.

1893
01:57:14,083 --> 01:57:15,542
We have to.

1894
01:57:16,958 --> 01:57:18,625
We will.

1895
01:57:43,292 --> 01:57:44,417
Boom!

1896
01:57:50,083 --> 01:57:51,542
All right, the glove's ready.

1897
01:57:52,333 --> 01:57:55,082
Question is, who's gonna
snap their freakin' fingers?

1898
01:57:55,083 --> 01:57:57,332
- I'll do it.
-  Excuse me?

1899
01:57:57,333 --> 01:57:58,457
It's okay.

1900
01:57:58,458 --> 01:57:59,416
Stop, stop. Slow down.

1901
01:57:59,417 --> 01:58:01,207
Thor. Just wait.

1902
01:58:01,208 --> 01:58:03,416
We haven't decided
who's gonna put that on yet.

1903
01:58:03,417 --> 01:58:05,166
I'm sorry. What, we're all
just sitting around

1904
01:58:05,167 --> 01:58:06,499
waiting for
the right opportunity?

1905
01:58:06,500 --> 01:58:07,791
We should at least discuss it.

1906
01:58:07,792 --> 01:58:09,541
Look, sitting here
staring at the thing

1907
01:58:09,542 --> 01:58:11,625
is not gonna bring
everybody back.

1908
01:58:12,667 --> 01:58:14,041
I'm the strongest
Avenger, okay?

1909
01:58:14,042 --> 01:58:15,749
So, this responsibility
falls upon me.

1910
01:58:15,750 --> 01:58:16,999
- Normally, you're right.
- It's my duty.

1911
01:58:17,000 --> 01:58:19,082
- It's not about that.
- It's not that.

1912
01:58:19,083 --> 01:58:20,875
-  Hey, buddy...
- Stop it! Just let me.

1913
01:58:23,875 --> 01:58:25,541
Just let me do it.

1914
01:58:25,542 --> 01:58:28,207
Just let me do something good.
Something right.

1915
01:58:28,208 --> 01:58:30,124
Look, it's not just the fact
that that glove is channeling

1916
01:58:30,125 --> 01:58:31,666
enough energy
to light up a continent.

1917
01:58:31,667 --> 01:58:33,832
I'm telling you.
You're in no condition.

1918
01:58:33,833 --> 01:58:37,041
What do you think is coursing
through my veins right now?

1919
01:58:37,042 --> 01:58:38,083
Cheez Whiz?

1920
01:58:40,625 --> 01:58:41,666
Lightning.

1921
01:58:41,667 --> 01:58:43,082
- Yeah.
- Lightning.

1922
01:58:43,083 --> 01:58:44,499
Lightning won't help you, pal.

1923
01:58:44,500 --> 01:58:46,458
It's gotta be me.

1924
01:58:47,792 --> 01:58:50,124
You saw what those stones
did to Thanos.

1925
01:58:50,125 --> 01:58:51,667
They almost killed him.

1926
01:58:53,083 --> 01:58:54,958
None of you could survive.

1927
01:58:55,667 --> 01:58:57,457
How do we know you will?

1928
01:58:57,458 --> 01:58:58,541
We don't.

1929
01:58:58,542 --> 01:59:01,416
But the radiation's
mostly gamma.

1930
01:59:04,833 --> 01:59:06,417
It's like...

1931
01:59:08,292 --> 01:59:10,208
I was made for this.

1932
01:59:29,125 --> 01:59:30,625
Good to go, yeah?

1933
01:59:32,750 --> 01:59:33,750
Let's do it.

1934
01:59:34,292 --> 01:59:35,374
Okay, remember,

1935
01:59:35,375 --> 01:59:37,124
everyone Thanos snapped away
five years ago,

1936
01:59:37,125 --> 01:59:39,749
you're just bringing them
back to now, today.

1937
01:59:39,750 --> 01:59:41,167
Don't change anything
from the last five years.

1938
01:59:42,583 --> 01:59:43,750
Got it.

1939
02:00:00,208 --> 02:00:01,374
Friday, do me a favor

1940
02:00:01,375 --> 02:00:03,082
and activate
Barn Door Protocol, will ya?

1941
02:00:03,083 --> 02:00:04,375
<i>Yes, boss.</i>

1942
02:00:12,958 --> 02:00:14,792
Everybody comes home.

1943
02:00:38,167 --> 02:00:39,749
Take it off! Take it off!

1944
02:00:39,750 --> 02:00:40,916
No, wait. Bruce, are you okay?

1945
02:00:42,042 --> 02:00:43,250
Talk to me, Banner.

1946
02:00:46,417 --> 02:00:47,417
I'm okay.

1947
02:00:47,917 --> 02:00:49,208
I'm okay.

1948
02:01:20,625 --> 02:01:21,750
Bruce!

1949
02:01:23,500 --> 02:01:25,083
Don't move him.

1950
02:01:31,958 --> 02:01:33,958
- Did it work?
- We're not sure. It's okay.

1951
02:02:20,417 --> 02:02:21,457
Honey.

1952
02:02:21,458 --> 02:02:22,582
Clint?

1953
02:02:22,583 --> 02:02:23,833
Honey.

1954
02:02:24,667 --> 02:02:26,000
Guys...

1955
02:02:28,458 --> 02:02:29,833
I think it worked.

1956
02:03:12,417 --> 02:03:14,374
I can't breathe!
I can't breathe!

1957
02:03:15,542 --> 02:03:17,333
Canopy, canopy, canopy.

1958
02:03:23,958 --> 02:03:25,750
Rhodey, Rocket,
get out of here.

1959
02:03:26,917 --> 02:03:28,458
Let me up! Let me up!

1960
02:03:29,208 --> 02:03:30,500
Come on!

1961
02:03:40,083 --> 02:03:40,917
Rhodey!

1962
02:03:42,708 --> 02:03:44,208
Huh?

1963
02:03:49,458 --> 02:03:51,207
Mayday, Mayday!
Does anybody copy?

1964
02:03:51,208 --> 02:03:52,666
We're on the lower level.
It's flooding!

1965
02:03:52,667 --> 02:03:54,541
What? What?

1966
02:03:54,542 --> 02:03:56,874
We are drowning!
Does anybody copy? Mayday!

1967
02:03:56,875 --> 02:03:59,207
Wait! I'm here!

1968
02:03:59,208 --> 02:04:00,708
I'm here. Can you hear me?

1969
02:04:20,333 --> 02:04:21,542
Cap?

1970
02:04:45,500 --> 02:04:46,625
Okay.

1971
02:05:05,875 --> 02:05:07,041
Daughter.

1972
02:05:07,042 --> 02:05:08,333
Yes, Father.

1973
02:05:10,208 --> 02:05:11,917
So, this is the future.

1974
02:05:12,583 --> 02:05:13,708
Well done.

1975
02:05:14,333 --> 02:05:15,999
Thank you, Father.

1976
02:05:16,000 --> 02:05:17,375
They suspected nothing.

1977
02:05:19,708 --> 02:05:21,167
The arrogant never do.

1978
02:05:24,125 --> 02:05:25,250
Go.

1979
02:05:26,208 --> 02:05:28,666
Find the stones,
bring them to me.

1980
02:05:28,667 --> 02:05:30,500
What will you do?

1981
02:05:31,833 --> 02:05:33,500
Wait.

1982
02:05:58,708 --> 02:06:00,375
Tell me something.

1983
02:06:01,500 --> 02:06:04,082
In the future,

1984
02:06:04,083 --> 02:06:05,958
what happens to you and me?

1985
02:06:08,250 --> 02:06:09,875
I try to kill you.

1986
02:06:11,583 --> 02:06:13,083
Several times.

1987
02:06:14,167 --> 02:06:16,291
But eventually

1988
02:06:16,292 --> 02:06:18,250
we become friends.

1989
02:06:19,750 --> 02:06:21,458
We become sisters.

1990
02:06:29,125 --> 02:06:30,333
Come on.

1991
02:06:32,375 --> 02:06:34,167
We can stop him.

1992
02:06:42,250 --> 02:06:43,666
Come on,
buddy, wake up!

1993
02:06:43,667 --> 02:06:45,583
That's my man.

1994
02:06:46,500 --> 02:06:48,542
You lose this again,
I'm keeping it.

1995
02:06:52,083 --> 02:06:53,416
What happened?

1996
02:06:53,417 --> 02:06:55,707
You mess with time,
it tends to mess back.

1997
02:06:55,708 --> 02:06:56,583
You'll see.

1998
02:07:18,667 --> 02:07:20,042
What's he been doing?

1999
02:07:21,958 --> 02:07:23,375
Absolutely nothing.

2000
02:07:25,125 --> 02:07:27,000
Where are the stones?

2001
02:07:27,500 --> 02:07:29,208
Somewhere under all this.

2002
02:07:30,583 --> 02:07:32,957
All I know is
he doesn't have 'em.

2003
02:07:32,958 --> 02:07:34,874
So, we keep it that way.

2004
02:07:34,875 --> 02:07:36,416
You know it's a trap, right?

2005
02:07:36,417 --> 02:07:37,916
Yeah.

2006
02:07:37,917 --> 02:07:39,250
I don't much care.

2007
02:07:40,000 --> 02:07:41,000
Good.

2008
02:07:41,958 --> 02:07:44,499
Just as long as
we're all in agreement.

2009
02:07:54,208 --> 02:07:56,208
Let's kill him
properly this time.

2010
02:08:05,583 --> 02:08:08,500
You could not live with
your own failure.

2011
02:08:10,000 --> 02:08:11,833
Where did that bring you?

2012
02:08:14,792 --> 02:08:16,667
Back to me.

2013
02:08:20,083 --> 02:08:22,917
I thought by
eliminating half of life

2014
02:08:23,667 --> 02:08:26,082
the other half would thrive.

2015
02:08:26,083 --> 02:08:27,542
But you've shown me

2016
02:08:28,708 --> 02:08:30,458
that's impossible.

2017
02:08:32,375 --> 02:08:35,832
And as long as there are those
that remember what was,

2018
02:08:35,833 --> 02:08:37,499
there will always be those

2019
02:08:37,500 --> 02:08:41,042
that are unable
to accept what can be.

2020
02:08:41,792 --> 02:08:43,042
They will resist.

2021
02:08:43,542 --> 02:08:45,458
Yep, we're
all kinds of stubborn.

2022
02:08:46,375 --> 02:08:47,958
I'm thankful.

2023
02:08:50,125 --> 02:08:52,041
Because now

2024
02:08:52,042 --> 02:08:54,167
I know what I must do.

2025
02:08:54,667 --> 02:08:57,624
I will shred this universe

2026
02:08:57,625 --> 02:08:59,792
down to its last atom.

2027
02:09:00,583 --> 02:09:02,291
And then,

2028
02:09:02,292 --> 02:09:04,750
with the stones
you've collected for me,

2029
02:09:05,542 --> 02:09:07,832
create a new one

2030
02:09:07,833 --> 02:09:10,207
teeming with life,

2031
02:09:10,208 --> 02:09:12,249
that knows not
what it has lost

2032
02:09:12,250 --> 02:09:14,625
but only what it has
been given.

2033
02:09:17,708 --> 02:09:19,125
A grateful universe.

2034
02:09:19,667 --> 02:09:21,124
Born out of blood.

2035
02:09:21,125 --> 02:09:22,917
They'll never know it.

2036
02:09:24,125 --> 02:09:27,042
Because you won't be
alive to tell them.

2037
02:09:41,625 --> 02:09:42,999
See you on
the other side, man.

2038
02:09:45,250 --> 02:09:47,624
Hang on! I'm coming!

2039
02:10:17,500 --> 02:10:18,500
Yeah!

2040
02:10:33,375 --> 02:10:35,082
Oh, hey.

2041
02:10:35,083 --> 02:10:36,792
I know you.

2042
02:10:39,708 --> 02:10:41,207
Father...

2043
02:10:41,208 --> 02:10:43,041
I have the stones.

2044
02:10:43,042 --> 02:10:43,958
What?

2045
02:10:45,333 --> 02:10:46,250
Stop.

2046
02:10:51,458 --> 02:10:52,875
You're betraying us?

2047
02:10:58,875 --> 02:11:00,167
You don't have to do this.

2048
02:11:03,000 --> 02:11:05,666
I am this.

2049
02:11:05,667 --> 02:11:07,583
No, you're not.

2050
02:11:08,083 --> 02:11:09,917
You've seen what we become.

2051
02:11:16,000 --> 02:11:18,208
Nebula, listen to her.

2052
02:11:19,667 --> 02:11:20,542
You can change.

2053
02:11:27,208 --> 02:11:28,708
He won't let me.

2054
02:11:30,333 --> 02:11:31,792
No!

2055
02:11:50,708 --> 02:11:52,124
Okay, Thor. Hit me.

2056
02:12:08,708 --> 02:12:10,000
<i>Boss, wake up!</i>

2057
02:13:01,250 --> 02:13:02,542
I knew it!

2058
02:14:24,833 --> 02:14:27,667
In all my years of conquest...

2059
02:14:28,958 --> 02:14:30,708
violence...

2060
02:14:31,750 --> 02:14:33,708
slaughter...

2061
02:14:34,833 --> 02:14:37,250
it was never personal.

2062
02:14:39,833 --> 02:14:41,917
But I'll tell you now...

2063
02:14:43,917 --> 02:14:45,374
what I'm about to do

2064
02:14:45,375 --> 02:14:50,167
to your stubborn,
annoying little planet...

2065
02:14:51,917 --> 02:14:54,125
I'm gonna enjoy it...

2066
02:14:55,042 --> 02:14:57,625
very, very much.

2067
02:16:00,833 --> 02:16:02,375
Hey, Cap, you read me?

2068
02:16:08,375 --> 02:16:10,667
Cap, it's Sam.
Can you hear me?

2069
02:16:14,667 --> 02:16:16,083
On your left.

2070
02:17:41,667 --> 02:17:42,999
Is that everyone?

2071
02:17:43,000 --> 02:17:45,333
What? You wanted more?

2072
02:18:11,833 --> 02:18:13,792
Avengers...

2073
02:18:18,917 --> 02:18:20,041
assemble.

2074
02:18:55,167 --> 02:18:56,417
Die!

2075
02:19:17,042 --> 02:19:19,792
No, no, give me that.
You have the little one.

2076
02:19:33,458 --> 02:19:34,458
Hey!

2077
02:19:35,292 --> 02:19:36,457
Holy cow!

2078
02:19:36,458 --> 02:19:37,916
You will not believe
what's been going on.

2079
02:19:37,917 --> 02:19:39,166
Do you remember
when we were in space?

2080
02:19:39,167 --> 02:19:40,832
And I got all dusty?

2081
02:19:40,833 --> 02:19:42,082
And I must've passed out,

2082
02:19:42,083 --> 02:19:43,666
because I woke up
and you were gone.

2083
02:19:43,667 --> 02:19:45,457
But Doctor Strange was there,
right? And he was like...

2084
02:19:45,458 --> 02:19:47,124
"It's been five years.
Come on, they need us."

2085
02:19:47,125 --> 02:19:48,624
And then he started doing the
yellow sparkly thing

2086
02:19:48,625 --> 02:19:49,957
- that he does all the time.
- He did? Oh, no.

2087
02:19:49,958 --> 02:19:52,333
What are you doing? Oh.

2088
02:19:56,125 --> 02:19:57,792
Oh, this is nice.

2089
02:20:19,542 --> 02:20:20,542
Gamora?

2090
02:20:29,958 --> 02:20:31,625
I thought I lost you.

2091
02:20:32,458 --> 02:20:33,458
Hi.

2092
02:20:35,042 --> 02:20:36,207
Ow.

2093
02:20:36,208 --> 02:20:39,125
Don't touch me!

2094
02:20:42,125 --> 02:20:44,124
You missed the first time.

2095
02:20:44,125 --> 02:20:46,125
Then you got 'em both
the second time.

2096
02:20:48,125 --> 02:20:49,374
This is the one?

2097
02:20:49,375 --> 02:20:50,541
Seriously?

2098
02:20:50,542 --> 02:20:52,624
Your choices were
him or a tree.

2099
02:21:03,333 --> 02:21:04,499
Cap!

2100
02:21:04,500 --> 02:21:06,250
What do you want me to do
with this damn thing?

2101
02:21:08,958 --> 02:21:11,166
Get those stones
as far away as possible!

2102
02:21:11,167 --> 02:21:15,499
No! We need to get 'em back
where they came from.

2103
02:21:15,500 --> 02:21:18,124
No way to get 'em back. Thanos
destroyed the quantum tunnel.

2104
02:21:18,125 --> 02:21:19,083
Hold on!

2105
02:21:20,958 --> 02:21:23,124
That wasn't
our only time machine.

2106
02:21:29,083 --> 02:21:31,000
Anyone see an ugly
brown van out there?

2107
02:21:31,542 --> 02:21:34,791
Yes! But you're not gonna like
where it's parked!

2108
02:21:34,792 --> 02:21:36,917
Scott, how long you need
to get that thing working?

2109
02:21:37,917 --> 02:21:39,332
Uh, maybe ten minutes.

2110
02:21:39,333 --> 02:21:41,124
Get it started.
We'll get the stones to you.

2111
02:21:41,125 --> 02:21:42,667
We're on it, Cap.

2112
02:21:52,417 --> 02:21:56,708
Hey. You said one out of
14 million, we win, yeah?

2113
02:21:57,625 --> 02:21:58,625
Tell me this is it.

2114
02:21:59,167 --> 02:22:01,082
If I tell you what happens,

2115
02:22:01,083 --> 02:22:02,250
it won't happen.

2116
02:22:05,833 --> 02:22:06,833
You better be right.

2117
02:22:15,250 --> 02:22:16,625
It's a mess back here.

2118
02:22:17,625 --> 02:22:18,625
It's dead.

2119
02:22:19,917 --> 02:22:21,582
- What?
- It's dead.

2120
02:22:21,583 --> 02:22:23,000
I have to hot-wire it.

2121
02:22:26,083 --> 02:22:27,292
Where's Nebula?

2122
02:22:28,417 --> 02:22:29,750
She's not responding.

2123
02:22:30,250 --> 02:22:31,458
Sire...

2124
02:22:41,208 --> 02:22:42,458
Clint!

2125
02:22:44,500 --> 02:22:45,625
Give it to me.

2126
02:23:07,875 --> 02:23:11,250
You took everything from me.

2127
02:23:11,750 --> 02:23:14,124
I don't even know who you are.

2128
02:23:14,125 --> 02:23:15,750
You will.

2129
02:23:38,167 --> 02:23:39,125
I got it!

2130
02:23:41,667 --> 02:23:43,292
Activate Instant Kill.

2131
02:24:06,167 --> 02:24:07,500
Rain fire!

2132
02:24:08,208 --> 02:24:10,291
But, sire, our troops!

2133
02:24:10,292 --> 02:24:12,042
Just do it!

2134
02:24:32,167 --> 02:24:34,542
Uh,
is anyone else seeing this?

2135
02:24:48,458 --> 02:24:49,832
I got this!

2136
02:24:49,833 --> 02:24:51,625
I got this.
Okay, I don't got this.

2137
02:24:52,125 --> 02:24:53,291
Help, somebody help!

2138
02:24:53,292 --> 02:24:55,167
Hey, Queens, heads up!

2139
02:25:05,208 --> 02:25:06,250
Hang on. I got you, kid.

2140
02:25:09,875 --> 02:25:11,207
Hey! Nice to meet you...

2141
02:25:11,208 --> 02:25:13,042
Oh, my God!

2142
02:25:49,583 --> 02:25:50,708
What the hell is this?

2143
02:25:51,500 --> 02:25:52,749
Friday, what
are they firing at?

2144
02:25:52,750 --> 02:25:54,625
<i>Something just
entered the upper atmosphere.</i>

2145
02:26:07,875 --> 02:26:10,042
Oh, yeah!

2146
02:26:29,917 --> 02:26:32,333
Danvers, we need
an assist here.

2147
02:26:41,083 --> 02:26:43,667
Hi, I'm Peter Parker.

2148
02:26:44,292 --> 02:26:45,874
Hey, Peter Parker.

2149
02:26:45,875 --> 02:26:47,082
You got something for me?

2150
02:26:53,167 --> 02:26:55,250
I don't know how you're gonna
get it through all of that.

2151
02:26:56,917 --> 02:26:58,333
Don't worry.

2152
02:26:59,208 --> 02:27:00,792
She's got help.

2153
02:29:48,458 --> 02:29:51,958
I am inevitable.

2154
02:30:12,042 --> 02:30:13,666
And I...

2155
02:30:15,250 --> 02:30:16,417
am...

2156
02:30:20,125 --> 02:30:21,624
Iron Man.

2157
02:32:20,208 --> 02:32:21,833
Mr. Stark?

2158
02:32:22,333 --> 02:32:24,582
Hey!

2159
02:32:24,583 --> 02:32:27,707
Mr. Stark. Can you hear me?

2160
02:32:27,708 --> 02:32:29,250
It's Peter.

2161
02:32:31,125 --> 02:32:32,167
Hey.

2162
02:32:33,208 --> 02:32:36,250
We won, Mr. Stark.

2163
02:32:38,083 --> 02:32:40,250
We won, Mr. Stark.

2164
02:32:41,875 --> 02:32:44,708
We won!
You did it, sir, you did it.

2165
02:32:45,208 --> 02:32:47,082
I'm sorry.

2166
02:32:47,083 --> 02:32:48,083
Tony.

2167
02:33:01,750 --> 02:33:02,957
Hey.

2168
02:33:02,958 --> 02:33:04,792
Hey, Pep.

2169
02:33:09,083 --> 02:33:10,332
Friday?

2170
02:33:10,333 --> 02:33:13,083
<i>Life functions critical.</i>

2171
02:33:21,667 --> 02:33:22,667
Tony?

2172
02:33:23,917 --> 02:33:25,000
Look at me.

2173
02:33:27,667 --> 02:33:29,583
We're gonna be okay.

2174
02:33:34,292 --> 02:33:36,167
You can rest now.

2175
02:35:21,625 --> 02:35:24,582
<i>Everybody wants
a happy ending, right?</i>

2176
02:35:24,583 --> 02:35:26,792
<i>But it doesn't always
roll that way.</i>

2177
02:35:28,875 --> 02:35:30,542
<i>Maybe this time.</i>

2178
02:35:32,125 --> 02:35:34,792
<i>I'm hoping
if you play this back...</i>

2179
02:35:36,458 --> 02:35:37,750
<i>it's in celebration.</i>

2180
02:35:39,042 --> 02:35:42,874
<i>I hope families are reunited.
I hope we get it back.</i>

2181
02:35:42,875 --> 02:35:43,957
<i>And something like</i>

2182
02:35:43,958 --> 02:35:45,750
<i>a normal version of
the planet has been restored.</i>

2183
02:35:46,875 --> 02:35:48,917
<i>If there ever was
such a thing.</i>

2184
02:35:49,500 --> 02:35:52,500
<i>God, what a world.
Universe, now.</i>

2185
02:35:53,458 --> 02:35:55,624
<i>If you told me ten years ago
that we weren't alone...</i>

2186
02:35:55,625 --> 02:35:57,624
<i>let alone to this extent,
I mean,</i>

2187
02:35:57,625 --> 02:35:59,416
<i>I wouldn't
have been surprised...</i>

2188
02:35:59,417 --> 02:36:01,249
<i>but come on, who knew?</i>

2189
02:36:01,250 --> 02:36:04,249
<i>The epic forces
of darkness and light</i>

2190
02:36:04,250 --> 02:36:06,041
<i>that have come into play.</i>

2191
02:36:06,042 --> 02:36:07,916
<i>And for better or worse...</i>

2192
02:36:07,917 --> 02:36:08,999
<i>that's the reality</i>

2193
02:36:09,000 --> 02:36:11,292
<i>Morgan's gonna have to
find a way to grow up in.</i>

2194
02:36:15,333 --> 02:36:16,416
So, I thought
I'd probably better

2195
02:36:16,417 --> 02:36:17,707
record a little greeting...

2196
02:36:17,708 --> 02:36:20,875
in the case of
an untimely death. On my part.

2197
02:36:21,417 --> 02:36:24,333
I mean, not that death
at any time isn't untimely.

2198
02:36:25,417 --> 02:36:26,499
This time travel thing

2199
02:36:26,500 --> 02:36:28,166
that we're gonna
try and pull off tomorrow...

2200
02:36:28,167 --> 02:36:29,541
it's got me scratching my head

2201
02:36:29,542 --> 02:36:31,124
about the survivability
of it all.

2202
02:36:31,125 --> 02:36:32,542
That's the thing.

2203
02:36:34,542 --> 02:36:36,624
Then again,
that's the hero gig, right?

2204
02:36:36,625 --> 02:36:37,667
Part of the journey
is the end.

2205
02:36:39,667 --> 02:36:40,874
What am I even tripping for?

2206
02:36:40,875 --> 02:36:41,957
Everything is gonna work out

2207
02:36:41,958 --> 02:36:44,958
exactly the way
it's supposed to.

2208
02:36:48,458 --> 02:36:50,083
I love you 3,000.

2209
02:39:04,917 --> 02:39:06,208
You know,
I wish there was a way

2210
02:39:07,375 --> 02:39:08,542
that I could let her know.

2211
02:39:11,167 --> 02:39:12,458
That we won.

2212
02:39:14,667 --> 02:39:15,875
We did it.

2213
02:39:19,958 --> 02:39:21,292
She knows.

2214
02:39:26,625 --> 02:39:28,708
They both do.

2215
02:39:37,667 --> 02:39:38,749
<i>How you doing, squirt?</i>

2216
02:39:38,750 --> 02:39:40,082
Good.

2217
02:39:40,083 --> 02:39:41,416
- You good?
- Mm-hmm.

2218
02:39:41,417 --> 02:39:44,208
- Good. You hungry?
- Mm-hmm.

2219
02:39:44,708 --> 02:39:45,708
What do you want?

2220
02:39:46,417 --> 02:39:47,833
Cheeseburgers.

2221
02:39:52,625 --> 02:39:55,041
You know,
your dad liked cheeseburgers.

2222
02:39:55,042 --> 02:39:56,458
Okay.

2223
02:39:59,042 --> 02:40:01,457
I'm gonna get you all
the cheeseburgers you want.

2224
02:40:01,458 --> 02:40:02,458
Okay.

2225
02:40:19,208 --> 02:40:20,874
So...

2226
02:40:20,875 --> 02:40:23,207
when can we expect you back?

2227
02:40:24,375 --> 02:40:26,417
Um, about that...

2228
02:40:26,958 --> 02:40:28,999
Thor, your people need a king.

2229
02:40:29,000 --> 02:40:30,916
No, they already have one.

2230
02:40:33,333 --> 02:40:34,542
That's funny.

2231
02:40:39,625 --> 02:40:41,417
Are you being serious?

2232
02:40:45,125 --> 02:40:46,499
It's time for me
to be who I am...

2233
02:40:46,500 --> 02:40:49,667
rather than
who I'm supposed to be.

2234
02:40:51,833 --> 02:40:53,542
But you, you're a leader.

2235
02:40:54,208 --> 02:40:55,917
That's who you are.

2236
02:40:58,417 --> 02:41:00,207
You know, I'd make
a lot of changes around here.

2237
02:41:00,208 --> 02:41:02,207
I'm counting on it...

2238
02:41:02,208 --> 02:41:03,708
Your Majesty.

2239
02:41:13,833 --> 02:41:15,000
What will you do?

2240
02:41:15,792 --> 02:41:17,374
I'm not sure.

2241
02:41:17,375 --> 02:41:19,957
For the first time
in a thousand years,

2242
02:41:19,958 --> 02:41:21,041
I have no path.

2243
02:41:21,042 --> 02:41:22,624
I do have a ride though.

2244
02:41:22,625 --> 02:41:24,374
Move it or lose it, hairbag.

2245
02:41:29,000 --> 02:41:30,625
Well, here we are!

2246
02:41:31,125 --> 02:41:32,667
Tree, good to see you.

2247
02:41:37,250 --> 02:41:40,458
The Asgardians of the Galaxy
back together again.

2248
02:41:40,958 --> 02:41:42,833
Where to first?

2249
02:41:43,958 --> 02:41:45,000
Hey.

2250
02:41:45,625 --> 02:41:47,749
Just so you know,
this is my ship still.

2251
02:41:47,750 --> 02:41:48,708
I'm in charge.

2252
02:41:49,292 --> 02:41:51,999
I know. I know.
Of course you are.

2253
02:41:52,000 --> 02:41:53,624
Of course.

2254
02:41:56,167 --> 02:41:58,874
See, you say, "Of course,"
but then you touch the map.

2255
02:41:58,875 --> 02:42:00,041
It makes you think that maybe

2256
02:42:00,042 --> 02:42:01,333
you didn't realize
I was in charge.

2257
02:42:02,000 --> 02:42:03,707
Quail, that's your own
insecurities in there.

2258
02:42:03,708 --> 02:42:04,624
Quail?

2259
02:42:04,625 --> 02:42:07,082
Okay? I am merely trying to be
of service and assisting.

2260
02:42:07,083 --> 02:42:08,457
Quill.

2261
02:42:08,458 --> 02:42:09,457
That's what I said.

2262
02:42:09,458 --> 02:42:11,999
You should fight one another
for the honor of leadership.

2263
02:42:12,000 --> 02:42:13,375
Sounds fair.

2264
02:42:14,292 --> 02:42:15,292
- Well...
- I--

2265
02:42:16,167 --> 02:42:18,707
- It's not necessary, okay?
- It's not.

2266
02:42:18,708 --> 02:42:19,791
I got some blasters,

2267
02:42:19,792 --> 02:42:21,249
unless you guys
wanna use knives.

2268
02:42:21,250 --> 02:42:23,624
Oh, yes! Please, use knives.

2269
02:42:23,625 --> 02:42:24,707
Yeah. Knives.

2270
02:42:24,708 --> 02:42:26,375
I am Groot.

2271
02:42:32,167 --> 02:42:33,707
Not necessary.

2272
02:42:33,708 --> 02:42:35,332
There shall be
no knifing one another.

2273
02:42:35,333 --> 02:42:38,333
Everybody knows
who's in charge.

2274
02:42:41,917 --> 02:42:43,125
Me.

2275
02:42:44,167 --> 02:42:45,000
Right?

2276
02:42:46,250 --> 02:42:48,416
Yes, you.

2277
02:42:48,417 --> 02:42:50,999
Of course! Of course.

2278
02:42:51,000 --> 02:42:52,667
Of course.

2279
02:42:54,375 --> 02:42:55,917
Remember...

2280
02:42:56,750 --> 02:42:57,916
you have to return the stones

2281
02:42:57,917 --> 02:42:59,166
to the exact moment
you got 'em...

2282
02:42:59,167 --> 02:43:00,082
or you're gonna open up

2283
02:43:00,083 --> 02:43:02,582
a bunch of
nasty alternative realities.

2284
02:43:02,583 --> 02:43:03,583
Don't worry, Bruce.

2285
02:43:04,125 --> 02:43:06,000
Clip all the branches.

2286
02:43:06,542 --> 02:43:08,292
You know, I tried.

2287
02:43:09,583 --> 02:43:11,166
When I had the gauntlet,
the stones,

2288
02:43:11,167 --> 02:43:13,792
I really tried
to bring her back.

2289
02:43:17,083 --> 02:43:18,749
I miss her, man.

2290
02:43:18,750 --> 02:43:20,083
Me too.

2291
02:43:24,167 --> 02:43:26,583
You know, if you want,
I could come with you.

2292
02:43:29,167 --> 02:43:30,625
You're a good man, Sam.

2293
02:43:31,167 --> 02:43:32,708
This one's on me, though.

2294
02:43:37,167 --> 02:43:39,083
Don't do anything stupid
till I get back.

2295
02:43:40,917 --> 02:43:42,332
How can I?

2296
02:43:42,333 --> 02:43:44,125
You're taking
all the stupid with you.

2297
02:43:51,708 --> 02:43:53,375
Gonna miss you, buddy.

2298
02:43:53,875 --> 02:43:55,375
It's gonna be okay, Buck.

2299
02:44:02,750 --> 02:44:04,791
How long is this gonna take?

2300
02:44:04,792 --> 02:44:07,542
For him, as long as he needs.
For us, five seconds.

2301
02:44:12,625 --> 02:44:14,041
You ready, Cap?

2302
02:44:14,042 --> 02:44:16,458
All right, we'll meet you
back here, okay?

2303
02:44:17,125 --> 02:44:18,250
You bet.

2304
02:44:19,750 --> 02:44:21,333
Going quantum.
Three...

2305
02:44:21,917 --> 02:44:22,750
two...

2306
02:44:23,417 --> 02:44:24,625
one.

2307
02:44:26,500 --> 02:44:28,707
And returning in five...

2308
02:44:28,708 --> 02:44:29,832
four...

2309
02:44:29,833 --> 02:44:31,707
three, two...

2310
02:44:31,708 --> 02:44:33,167
one.

2311
02:44:40,417 --> 02:44:41,582
Where is he?

2312
02:44:41,583 --> 02:44:43,499
I don't know. He blew
right by his time stamp.

2313
02:44:43,500 --> 02:44:44,958
He should be here.

2314
02:44:50,458 --> 02:44:51,541
Well, get him back.

2315
02:44:51,542 --> 02:44:52,832
- I'm trying.
- Get him the hell back.

2316
02:44:52,833 --> 02:44:54,708
- Hey, I said I'm trying.
- Sam.

2317
02:45:18,667 --> 02:45:20,250
Go ahead.

2318
02:45:38,125 --> 02:45:38,958
Cap?

2319
02:45:41,292 --> 02:45:43,042
Hi, Sam.

2320
02:45:46,042 --> 02:45:49,083
So, did something go wrong
or did something go right?

2321
02:45:51,208 --> 02:45:55,042
Well, after I put
the stones back, I thought...

2322
02:45:56,167 --> 02:45:57,500
maybe...

2323
02:45:58,000 --> 02:46:02,500
I'll try some of that life
Tony was telling me to get.

2324
02:46:04,792 --> 02:46:06,917
How'd that work out for ya?

2325
02:46:09,417 --> 02:46:10,833
It was beautiful.

2326
02:46:12,167 --> 02:46:14,041
Good. I'm happy for you.

2327
02:46:14,042 --> 02:46:15,083
Truly.

2328
02:46:15,833 --> 02:46:17,125
Thank you.

2329
02:46:18,458 --> 02:46:19,874
Only thing bumming me out...

2330
02:46:19,875 --> 02:46:20,957
is the fact I have to live

2331
02:46:20,958 --> 02:46:23,458
in a world
without Captain America.

2332
02:46:24,083 --> 02:46:25,083
Oh, well...

2333
02:46:27,250 --> 02:46:29,250
That reminds me.

2334
02:46:38,542 --> 02:46:39,750
Try it on.

2335
02:47:05,250 --> 02:47:06,750
How does it feel?

2336
02:47:09,333 --> 02:47:11,042
Like it's someone else's.

2337
02:47:14,083 --> 02:47:15,250
It isn't.

2338
02:47:28,583 --> 02:47:30,167
Thank you.

2339
02:47:31,875 --> 02:47:33,167
I'll do my best.

2340
02:47:38,542 --> 02:47:40,458
That's why it's yours.

2341
02:47:42,167 --> 02:47:43,542
You wanna tell me about her?

2342
02:47:50,125 --> 02:47:51,542
No.

2343
02:47:52,042 --> 02:47:54,167
No, I don't think I will.

2344
02:49:09,833 --> 02:49:10,750
Hi.

2345
02:49:11,833 --> 02:49:13,041
Can I help you?

2346
02:49:13,042 --> 02:49:14,042
No.

2347
02:49:17,000 --> 02:49:18,375
But I believe I can help you.

2348
02:49:20,042 --> 02:49:22,083
Both of you.

2349
02:54:00,417 --> 02:54:01,958
This is Dr. Bruce Banner.

2350
02:54:04,208 --> 02:54:05,666
Recently, I suffered, um,

2351
02:54:05,667 --> 02:54:08,083
my first incident
in over a decade.

2352
02:54:09,417 --> 02:54:11,457
Since then, I've been
in self-containment

2353
02:54:11,458 --> 02:54:14,541
in a joint base
military complex...

2354
02:54:17,875 --> 02:54:20,249
...two miles under
the surface of the earth.

2355
02:54:20,250 --> 02:54:22,375
The Hulk is not
getting out of here.

2356
02:54:23,458 --> 02:54:24,958
And no one else is getting in.

2357
02:54:26,292 --> 02:54:27,292
Um...

2358
02:54:28,875 --> 02:54:30,874
During my time here,

2359
02:54:30,875 --> 02:54:33,166
I've actually been
experimenting...

2360
02:54:36,000 --> 02:54:39,041
I've been experimenting with
a new gamma suppression serum,

2361
02:54:39,042 --> 02:54:39,957
and my...

2362
02:54:39,958 --> 02:54:41,500
...my early results
have been...

2363
02:54:43,417 --> 02:54:44,875
have been quite promising.

2364
02:54:45,583 --> 02:54:47,957
So today, I'd like to
demonstrate to you

2365
02:54:47,958 --> 02:54:49,791
some of my findings here.

2366
02:54:54,542 --> 02:54:55,542
No.

2367
02:54:58,333 --> 02:54:59,457
Who are you?

2368
02:54:59,458 --> 02:55:01,041
Mr. Banner.

2369
02:55:01,042 --> 02:55:02,332
What are you doing here?

2370
02:55:02,333 --> 02:55:04,249
I'm here to collect you.

2371
02:56:27,000 --> 02:56:30,707
<i>Welcome to the
Time Variance Authority.</i>

2372
02:56:30,708 --> 02:56:33,083
<i>"TVA" for short.</i>

2373
02:56:33,750 --> 02:56:37,291
<i>There's a whole mess of
universes out there.</i>

2374
02:56:37,292 --> 02:56:40,624
<i>Our job is keeping 'em
tidy and safe.</i>

2375
02:56:40,625 --> 02:56:44,166
<i>So, do us a favor,
and stay in your universe.</i>

2376
02:56:44,167 --> 02:56:45,291
-  Morning.
-  Morning.

2377
02:56:45,292 --> 02:56:47,249
<i>So we don't have to
hunt you down like a dog.</i>

2378
02:56:47,250 --> 02:56:48,750
-  How are you doing?
<i>- Bye, now.</i>

2379
02:56:51,083 --> 02:56:52,708
That doesn't look too good.

2380
02:56:54,708 --> 02:56:55,874
It's a level one incursion.

2381
02:56:55,875 --> 02:57:00,332
Universes 10005 and 1127
are about to collide.

2382
02:57:00,333 --> 02:57:02,124
Okay. Well,

2383
02:57:02,125 --> 02:57:05,457
I did not read about
this in the scouting report,

2384
02:57:05,458 --> 02:57:06,874
or I don't remember.

2385
02:57:06,875 --> 02:57:10,624
Could it have slipped through
the cracks for old Mobius?

2386
02:57:10,625 --> 02:57:11,792
Are those missiles?

2387
02:57:13,917 --> 02:57:15,417
Are they firing at each other?

2388
02:57:16,458 --> 02:57:17,916
Each earth is trying to
take out the other

2389
02:57:17,917 --> 02:57:19,457
before they collide.

2390
02:57:19,458 --> 02:57:21,291
Call over to Forecasting.

2391
02:57:21,292 --> 02:57:24,082
Find out why we didn't
get a heads-up on this.

2392
02:57:24,083 --> 02:57:26,000
-  I'm on it.
- Wait. We've got another one.

2393
02:57:31,208 --> 02:57:33,582
No, that's a glitch.
Here, reset this.

2394
02:57:33,583 --> 02:57:35,374
- Reset this.
- We have a third.

2395
02:57:42,208 --> 02:57:44,416
Put us on full alert now.
Give me a count.

2396
02:57:44,417 --> 02:57:47,124
- Uh, twenty universes done.
- I've got a hundred.

2397
02:57:47,125 --> 02:57:48,582
300.

2398
02:57:48,583 --> 02:57:50,375
3,000.

2399
02:57:58,042 --> 02:58:00,082
The Multiverse is collapsing.

